<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Preliminaries and Reviews</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We summarize the key notations and assumptions used in our theorems. The data distribution is <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>, and the model is <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is restricted to a parameter space <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. The vector Gaussian channel follows <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}_{t}=\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}+\sigma_{t}\mathbf{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐍</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}_{t}=\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}+\sigma_{t}\mathbf{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> controls the time-dependent coefficient, <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> represents the time horizon, and <math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{N}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{n};0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐍</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{N}\sim\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{n};0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math> is Gaussian noise. The input <math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\sim p(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\sim p(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>, and the output <math id="A1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{t}\sim p(\mathbf{y}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{t}\sim p(\mathbf{y}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, with both as column vectors of appropriate dimensions.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Notations</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we are working on the Euclidean space <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote the <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-inner product between vectors <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}=(u_{1},\dots,u_{d}),\mathbf{v}=(v_{1},\dots,v_{d})\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}=(u_{1},\dots,u_{d}),\mathbf{v}=(v_{1},\dots,v_{d})\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}^{\top}\mathbf{v}=\langle\mathbf{u},\mathbf{v}\rangle=\sum_{i=1}^{D}u_{i}v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}^{\top}\mathbf{v}=\langle\mathbf{u},\mathbf{v}\rangle=\sum_{i=1}^{D}u_{i}v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For a symmetric matrix <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math>, the notation <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math> means <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is positive semidefinite, i.e., <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}^{\top}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{u}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐀𝐮</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}^{\top}\mathbf{A}\mathbf{u}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}\in\mathbb{R}^{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>R</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}\in\mathbb{R}^{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. For symmetric matrices <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A},\mathbf{B}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A},\mathbf{B}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math>, the notation <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}\succeq\mathbf{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⪰</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}\succeq\mathbf{B}</annotation></semantics></math> means <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}-\mathbf{B}\succeq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐁</mi></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}-\mathbf{B}\succeq 0</annotation></semantics></math> is positive semidefinite. Throughout, let <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{I}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐈</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{I}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the identity matrix.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For a differentiable function <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{D}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{D}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla f(\mathbf{x})\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla f(\mathbf{x})\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the gradient vector at <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> of the partial derivatives: <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\nabla f(\mathbf{x}))_{i}=\frac{\partial f(\mathbf{x})}{\partial\mathbf{x}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\nabla f(\mathbf{x}))_{i}=\frac{\partial f(\mathbf{x})}{\partial\mathbf{x}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}f(\mathbf{x})\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}f(\mathbf{x})\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> be the Hessian matrix of second partial derivatives: <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\nabla^{2}f(\mathbf{x}))_{i,j}=\frac{\partial^{2}f(\mathbf{x})}{\partial\mathbf{x}_{i}\partial\mathbf{x}_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\nabla^{2}f(\mathbf{x}))_{i,j}=\frac{\partial^{2}f(\mathbf{x})}{\partial\mathbf{x}_{i}\partial\mathbf{x}_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta f(\mathbf{x})=\operatorname{Tr}(\nabla^{2}f(\mathbf{x}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta f(\mathbf{x})=\operatorname{Tr}(\nabla^{2}f(\mathbf{x}))</annotation></semantics></math> be the Laplacian. We use <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote all continuous functions, and let <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the family of functions with continuous <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th order derivatives.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For a vector field <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}:\mathbb{R}^{D}\to\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}:\mathbb{R}^{D}\to\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}(\mathbf{x})=(\mathbf{v}_{1}(\mathbf{x}),\dots,\mathbf{v}_{d}(\mathbf{x}))\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}(\mathbf{x})=(\mathbf{v}_{1}(\mathbf{x}),\dots,\mathbf{v}_{d}(\mathbf{x}))\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\mathbf{v}:\mathbb{R}^{D}\to\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\mathbf{v}:\mathbb{R}^{D}\to\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> be the Jacobian matrix of mixed partial derivatives: <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\nabla\mathbf{v}(\mathbf{x}))_{i,j}=\frac{\partial\mathbf{v}_{i}(\mathbf{x})}{\partial\mathbf{x}_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\nabla\mathbf{v}(\mathbf{x}))_{i,j}=\frac{\partial\mathbf{v}_{i}(\mathbf{x})}{\partial\mathbf{x}_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\cdot\mathbf{v}:\mathbb{R}^{D}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\cdot\mathbf{v}:\mathbb{R}^{D}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be the divergence of <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}</annotation></semantics></math>, defined by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\nabla\cdot\mathbf{v})(\mathbf{x})=\sum_{i=1}^{D}\frac{\partial\mathbf{v}_{i}(\mathbf{x})}{\partial\mathbf{x}_{i}}=\operatorname{Tr}(\nabla\mathbf{v}(\mathbf{x}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝐯</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\nabla\cdot\mathbf{v})(\mathbf{x})=\sum_{i=1}^{D}\frac{\partial\mathbf{v}_{i}(\mathbf{x})}{\partial\mathbf{x}_{i}}=\operatorname{Tr}(\nabla\mathbf{v}(\mathbf{x})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{r}\subset\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{r}\subset\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> be the region (an <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional ball) bounded by the closed, piecewise-smooth, oriented surface <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the <em id="A1.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="A1.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>-sphere</em> of radius <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> centered at the origin. At any point <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}\in S_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}\in S_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, the symbol <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under the notation <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{s}_{r}=\|d\mathbf{s}_{r}\|\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{s}_{r}=\|d\mathbf{s}_{r}\|\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Definitions</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{D})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the space of probability distributions <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> which are absolutely continuous with respect to the Lebesgue measure and have a finite second moment <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\rho}[\|\mathbf{X}\|^{2}]&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\rho}[\|\mathbf{X}\|^{2}]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. We identify a probability distribution <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{D})</annotation></semantics></math> with its probability density function with respect to the Lebesgue measure, which we also denote by <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{D}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{D}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(x)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(x)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\rho(x)dx=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\rho(x)dx=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We say <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> is absolutely continuous with respect to another distribution <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted by <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\ll\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\ll\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu(\mathbf{A})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu(\mathbf{A})=0</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(\mathbf{A})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\mathbf{A})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>; if <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> both have density functions, then <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\ll\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\ll\nu</annotation></semantics></math> means <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu(\mathbf{x})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu(\mathbf{x})=0</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(\mathbf{x})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\mathbf{x})=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}(\cdot):\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{D})\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(\cdot):\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{D})\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be the differential Shannon entropy:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{H}(\rho)=-\mathbb{E}_{\rho}[\log\rho]=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\rho(\mathbf{x})\log\rho(\mathbf{x})\,d\mathbf{x}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(\rho)=-\mathbb{E}_{\rho}[\log\rho]=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\rho(\mathbf{x})\log\rho(\mathbf{x})\,d\mathbf{x}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}(\cdot):\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{D})\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}(\cdot):\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^{D})\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be the Fisher information:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}(\rho)=\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\left[\|\nabla\log\rho\|^{2}\right]=-\mathbb{E}_{\rho}[\Delta\log\rho]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}(\rho)=\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\left[\|\nabla\log\rho\|^{2}\right]=-\mathbb{E}_{\rho}[\Delta\log\rho],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and we define <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}(\rho)=+\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}(\rho)=+\infty</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> does not have a differentiable density. The second equality in the definition of <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}(\rho)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}(\rho)</annotation></semantics></math> above follows by integration by parts.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Note that the expression in (<a href="#A1.E15" title="In Definition 2. ‣ A.2 Definitions ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) is a special case (with respect to a translation parameter) which does not involve an explicit parameter as in its most general definition.<span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
              
              
              
            The parameterized Fisher information matrix is defined with respect to a parameter <math id="footnote3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}\in\mathbf{\Theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝚯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}\in\mathbf{\Theta}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="footnote3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}(\rho)\equiv\mathbb{E}_{\rho}[\nabla_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\log\rho(\mathbf{x};\boldsymbol{\theta})\,\nabla_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}^{\top}\log\rho(\mathbf{x};\boldsymbol{\theta})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}(\rho)\equiv\mathbb{E}_{\rho}[\nabla_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}\log\rho(\mathbf{x};\boldsymbol{\theta})\,\nabla_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}^{\top}\log\rho(\mathbf{x};\boldsymbol{\theta})]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For probability distributions <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\ll\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\ll\nu</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, the Kullback-Leibler (KL) divergence or the relative entropy of <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\text{KL}}(\rho\|\nu)=\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\left[\log\frac{\rho}{\nu}\right]=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\rho(\mathbf{x})\log\frac{\rho(\mathbf{x})}{\nu(\mathbf{x})}\,d\mathbf{x}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mi>ν</mi></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{KL}}(\rho\|\nu)=\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\left[\log\frac{\rho}{\nu}\right]=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\rho(\mathbf{x})\log\frac{\rho(\mathbf{x})}{\nu(\mathbf{x})}\,d\mathbf{x}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For probability distributions <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\ll\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≪</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\ll\nu</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, the mismatched entropy or the cross entropy of <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}(\rho,\nu)=-\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\left[\log\nu\right]=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\rho(\mathbf{x})\frac{1}{\log\nu(\mathbf{x})}d\mathbf{x}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(\rho,\nu)=-\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\left[\log\nu\right]=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\rho(\mathbf{x})\frac{1}{\log\nu(\mathbf{x})}d\mathbf{x}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 5</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> have differentiable density functions, then the relative Fisher information of <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I(\rho\|\nu)=\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\left[\left\|\nabla\log\frac{\rho}{\nu}\right\|^{2}\right]=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\rho(\mathbf{x})\left\|\nabla\log\frac{\rho(\mathbf{x})}{\nu(\mathbf{x})}\right\|^{2}\,d\mathbf{x}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mi>ν</mi></mfrac><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\rho\|\nu)=\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\left[\left\|\nabla\log\frac{\rho}{\nu}\right\|^{2}\right]=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\rho(\mathbf{x})\left\|\nabla\log\frac{\rho(\mathbf{x})}{\nu(\mathbf{x})}\right\|^{2}\,d\mathbf{x}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We recall that the KL divergence, <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\text{KL}}(\cdot\|\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{KL}}(\cdot\|\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, corresponds to the Bregman divergence of the negative entropy. Similarly, the relative Fisher information (RFI), <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I(\cdot\|\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\cdot\|\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, can be viewed as the Bregman divergence of the Fisher information. Moreover, half of the RFI is equivalent to score matching, as defined in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Standard Diffusion Models</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider a Gaussian diffusion process <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>, which starts from clean data <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and defines a sequence of progressively noisier versions, denoted by channel outputs <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> runs from 0 (least noisy) to 1 (most noisy). In the sampling process, given <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, we uniformly discretise the time interval into <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> timesteps, each of width <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/T</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t(i)=i/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t(i)=i/T</annotation></semantics></math> denote the current timestep and <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(i)=(i-1)/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(i)=(i-1)/T</annotation></semantics></math> the preceding one <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Forward Process.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The forward process is defined by a conditional Gaussian distribution:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})=\mathcal{N}(\alpha_{t}\mathbf{x},\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})=\mathcal{N}(\alpha_{t}\mathbf{x},\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and, by the Markov property,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{y}_{s})=\mathcal{N}(\alpha_{t|s}\mathbf{y}_{s},\sigma_{t|s}^{2}\mathbf{I})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{y}_{s})=\mathcal{N}(\alpha_{t|s}\mathbf{y}_{s},\sigma_{t|s}^{2}\mathbf{I}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t|s}=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{\alpha_{s}},\quad\sigma_{t|s}^{2}=\sigma_{t}^{2}-\frac{\alpha_{t|s}^{2}}{\sigma_{s}^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t|s}=\frac{\alpha_{t}}{\alpha_{s}},\quad\sigma_{t|s}^{2}=\sigma_{t}^{2}-\frac{\alpha_{t|s}^{2}}{\sigma_{s}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reverse Process.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As established in prior work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>, <a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>, <a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">68</a>]</cite>, the conditional distribution <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{y}_{s}|\mathbf{y}_{t},\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{y}_{s}|\mathbf{y}_{t},\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> is also Gaussian:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{y}_{s}|\mathbf{y}_{t},\mathbf{x})=\mathcal{N}\left(\frac{\alpha_{t|s}\sigma_{s}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mathbf{y}_{t}+\frac{\sigma_{t|s}^{2}\alpha_{s}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mathbf{x},\ \frac{\sigma_{s}^{2}\sigma_{t|s}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mathbf{I}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{y}_{s}|\mathbf{y}_{t},\mathbf{x})=\mathcal{N}\left(\frac{\alpha_{t|s}\sigma_{s}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mathbf{y}_{t}+\frac{\sigma_{t|s}^{2}\alpha_{s}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mathbf{x},\ \frac{\sigma_{s}^{2}\sigma_{t|s}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mathbf{I}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">As the ground truth <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> is not available during the reverse process, it is approximated by a neural network <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{x}}(\mathbf{y}_{t},t;{\boldsymbol{\theta}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{x}}(\mathbf{y}_{t},t;{\boldsymbol{\theta}})</annotation></semantics></math>, parameterised by <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. The learned reverse kernel becomes:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{y}_{s}|\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})=\mathcal{N}\left(\frac{\alpha_{t|s}\sigma_{s}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mathbf{y}_{t}+\frac{\sigma_{t|s}^{2}\alpha_{s}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\hat{\mathbf{x}}(\mathbf{y}_{t},t;{\boldsymbol{\theta}}),\ \frac{\sigma_{s}^{2}\sigma_{t|s}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mathbf{I}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{y}_{s}|\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})=\mathcal{N}\left(\frac{\alpha_{t|s}\sigma_{s}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mathbf{y}_{t}+\frac{\sigma_{t|s}^{2}\alpha_{s}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\hat{\mathbf{x}}(\mathbf{y}_{t},t;{\boldsymbol{\theta}}),\ \frac{\sigma_{s}^{2}\sigma_{t|s}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mathbf{I}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Lemmas</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we introduce all Lemmas in order to prove the Theorems in the next section.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> be a random vector with density <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Suppose <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Psi}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚿</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Psi}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is an arbitrary independent random vector with zero mean and identity matrix <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐈</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define <math id="Thmlemma1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{X}}=\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}+\sigma_{t}\,\boldsymbol{\Psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚿</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{X}}=\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}+\sigma_{t}\,\boldsymbol{\Psi}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="Thmlemma1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the density of <math id="Thmlemma1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then for every <math id="Thmlemma1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{x}}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{x}}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, as <math id="Thmlemma1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}_{t}\rightarrow 0^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}_{t}\rightarrow 0^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\bigg|_{\sigma^{2}_{t}=0^{+}}=\frac{1}{2}\Delta p(\mathbf{x})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\bigg|_{\sigma^{2}_{t}=0^{+}}=\frac{1}{2}\Delta p(\mathbf{x}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{\mathbf{x}}=\sum_{j=1}^{D}\frac{\partial^{2}}{\partial(x_{j})^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{\mathbf{x}}=\sum_{j=1}^{D}\frac{\partial^{2}}{\partial(x_{j})^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the usual Laplacian in <math id="Thmlemma1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Formula (<a href="#A1.E19" title="In Lemma 1. ‣ A.4 Lemmas ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) allows the derivative w.r.t. the energy of the perturbation <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to be transformed to the second derivative of the original pdf. In what followed we provide the proof for Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ A.4 Lemmas ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> which is slightly different than that in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>]</cite>. Note that Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ A.4 Lemmas ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> does not require the distribution of the perturbation to be symmetric as is required in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the probability density function of the random vector <math id="A1.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{X}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and define its characteristic function as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(\mathbf{k},\sigma_{t}^{2})=\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(i\,\mathbf{k}^{\top}\tilde{\mathbf{X}}\right)\right],\quad\mathbf{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\mathbf{k},\sigma_{t}^{2})=\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(i\,\mathbf{k}^{\top}\tilde{\mathbf{X}}\right)\right],\quad\mathbf{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Given that <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by</span></p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{X}}=\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}+\sigma_{t}\boldsymbol{\Psi}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚿</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{X}}=\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}+\sigma_{t}\boldsymbol{\Psi},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Psi}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent, the characteristic function factorises as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\phi(\mathbf{k},\sigma_{t}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\phi(\mathbf{k},\sigma_{t}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[e^{i\mathbf{k}^{\top}(\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}+\sigma_{t}\boldsymbol{\Psi})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚿</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[e^{i\mathbf{k}^{\top}(\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}+\sigma_{t}\boldsymbol{\Psi})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[e^{i\mathbf{k}^{\top}\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[e^{i\mathbf{k}^{\top}\sigma_{t}\boldsymbol{\Psi}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚿</mi></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[e^{i\mathbf{k}^{\top}\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[e^{i\mathbf{k}^{\top}\sigma_{t}\boldsymbol{\Psi}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\underbrace{\phi(\alpha_{t}\mathbf{k},0)}_{\text{characteristic function of }\mathbf{X}}\times\underbrace{\mathbb{E}\left[e^{i\mathbf{k}^{\top}\sigma_{t}\boldsymbol{\Psi}}\right]}_{\text{characteristic function of }\sigma_{t}\boldsymbol{\Psi}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐤</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>characteristic function of </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></munder><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚿</mi></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>characteristic function of </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚿</mi></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\underbrace{\phi(\alpha_{t}\mathbf{k},0)}_{\text{characteristic function of }\mathbf{X}}\times\underbrace{\mathbb{E}\left[e^{i\mathbf{k}^{\top}\sigma_{t}\boldsymbol{\Psi}}\right]}_{\text{characteristic function of }\sigma_{t}\boldsymbol{\Psi}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Expanding the exponential function via Taylor’s theorem gives</span></p>
<table id="A1.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{i\mathbf{k}^{\top}\sigma_{t}\boldsymbol{\Psi}}=1+i\sigma_{t}(\mathbf{k}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\Psi})-\frac{(\sigma_{t}\mathbf{k}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\Psi})^{2}}{2!}+O(\sigma_{t}^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚿</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚿</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚿</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{i\mathbf{k}^{\top}\sigma_{t}\boldsymbol{\Psi}}=1+i\sigma_{t}(\mathbf{k}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\Psi})-\frac{(\sigma_{t}\mathbf{k}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\Psi})^{2}}{2!}+O(\sigma_{t}^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\boldsymbol{\Psi}]=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝚿</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\boldsymbol{\Psi}]=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}[\boldsymbol{\Psi}]=\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝚿</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}[\boldsymbol{\Psi}]=\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{k}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\Psi}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚿</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathbf{k}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\Psi}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[(\mathbf{k}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\Psi})^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚿</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[(\mathbf{k}^{\top}\boldsymbol{\Psi})^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbf{k}^{\top}\mathbb{E}[\boldsymbol{\Psi}\boldsymbol{\Psi}^{\top}]\mathbf{k}=\|\mathbf{k}\|^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝚿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐤</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐤</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbf{k}^{\top}\mathbb{E}[\boldsymbol{\Psi}\boldsymbol{\Psi}^{\top}]\mathbf{k}=\|\mathbf{k}\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectations, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[e^{i\mathbf{k}^{\top}\sigma_{t}\boldsymbol{\Psi}}\right]=1-\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{2}\|\mathbf{k}\|^{2}+o(\sigma_{t}^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚿</mi></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐤</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[e^{i\mathbf{k}^{\top}\sigma_{t}\boldsymbol{\Psi}}\right]=1-\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{2}\|\mathbf{k}\|^{2}+o(\sigma_{t}^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, the characteristic function satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(\mathbf{k},\sigma_{t}^{2})=\phi(\alpha_{t}\mathbf{k},0)\left(1-\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{2}\|\mathbf{k}\|^{2}+o(\sigma_{t}^{2})\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐤</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐤</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\mathbf{k},\sigma_{t}^{2})=\phi(\alpha_{t}\mathbf{k},0)\left(1-\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{2}\|\mathbf{k}\|^{2}+o(\sigma_{t}^{2})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recalling the inverse Fourier transform, the probability density function is given by</span></p>
<table id="A1.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\sigma_{t}^{2}}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})=\frac{1}{(2\pi)^{D}}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}e^{-i\mathbf{k}^{\top}\tilde{\mathbf{x}}}\phi(\mathbf{k},\sigma_{t}^{2})d\mathbf{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐤</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\sigma_{t}^{2}}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})=\frac{1}{(2\pi)^{D}}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}e^{-i\mathbf{k}^{\top}\tilde{\mathbf{x}}}\phi(\mathbf{k},\sigma_{t}^{2})d\mathbf{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting the expansion of <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(\mathbf{k},\sigma_{t}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\mathbf{k},\sigma_{t}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\sigma_{t}^{2}}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})=\frac{1}{(2\pi)^{D}}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}e^{-i\mathbf{k}^{\top}\tilde{\mathbf{x}}}\phi(\alpha_{t}\mathbf{k},0)\left(1-\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{2}\|\mathbf{k}\|^{2}+o(\sigma_{t}^{2})\right)d\mathbf{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐤</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐤</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐤</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\sigma_{t}^{2}}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})=\frac{1}{(2\pi)^{D}}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}e^{-i\mathbf{k}^{\top}\tilde{\mathbf{x}}}\phi(\alpha_{t}\mathbf{k},0)\left(1-\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{2}\|\mathbf{k}\|^{2}+o(\sigma_{t}^{2})\right)d\mathbf{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since</span></p>
<table id="A1.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})=\frac{1}{(2\pi)^{D}}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}e^{-i\mathbf{k}^{\top}\tilde{\mathbf{x}}}\phi(\alpha_{t}\mathbf{k},0)d\mathbf{k}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐤</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐤</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐤</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})=\frac{1}{(2\pi)^{D}}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}e^{-i\mathbf{k}^{\top}\tilde{\mathbf{x}}}\phi(\alpha_{t}\mathbf{k},0)d\mathbf{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">it follows that the difference <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\sigma_{t}^{2}}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})-p_{0}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\sigma_{t}^{2}}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})-p_{0}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to multiplying <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(\alpha_{t}\mathbf{k},0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐤</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(\alpha_{t}\mathbf{k},0)</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{2}\|\mathbf{k}\|^{2}+o(\sigma_{t}^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐤</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{2}\|\mathbf{k}\|^{2}+o(\sigma_{t}^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">A standard result from Fourier analysis states that multiplication by <math id="A1.SS4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\|\mathbf{k}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐤</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\|\mathbf{k}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> in the Fourier domain corresponds to the application of the Laplacian <math id="A1.SS4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> in the spatial domain, defined as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathbf{x}}=\sum_{j=1}^{D}\frac{\partial^{2}}{\partial x_{j}^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>𝐱</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover><mfrac><msup><mo>∂</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathbf{x}}=\sum_{j=1}^{D}\frac{\partial^{2}}{\partial x_{j}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, for small <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A1.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\sigma_{t}^{2}}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})=p_{0}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})+\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{2}\Delta_{\tilde{\mathbf{x}}}p_{0}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})+o(\sigma_{t}^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\sigma_{t}^{2}}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})=p_{0}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})+\frac{\sigma_{t}^{2}}{2}\Delta_{\tilde{\mathbf{x}}}p_{0}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})+o(\sigma_{t}^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> in the absence of noise, this completes the proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ A.4 Lemmas ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Vanishing boundary flux)<span id="Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For an arbitrary input distribution <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>, an assumed input distribution <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝛉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> and a vector Gaussian channel <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})=\mathcal{N}(\alpha_{t}\mathbf{x},\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})=\mathcal{N}(\alpha_{t}\mathbf{x},\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2.1 Incremental Gaussian Channel and Maximum Likelihood Estimation ‣ 2 Background ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), denote the corresponding output densities by <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{y}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{y}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝛉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> at time <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{r}:=\{\mathbf{y}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}:\|\mathbf{y}\|\leq r\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{r}:=\{\mathbf{y}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}:\|\mathbf{y}\|\leq r\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the closed <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>-ball and let <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{r}:=\partial B_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{r}:=\partial B_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D\!-\!1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.052em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D\!-\!1)</annotation></semantics></math>-sphere with outward unit normal <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})=\mathbf{y}/\|\mathbf{y}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})=\mathbf{y}/\|\mathbf{y}\|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Assume <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{y}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{y}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝛉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> with well-defined <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathbf{y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>𝐲</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathbf{y}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and that <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{p}\!\big[\log q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\big]&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝛉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{p}\!\big[\log q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\big]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then the boundary integrals</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\lim_{r\to\infty}\int_{S_{r}}\log q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\,\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\cdot\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y}_{t})\,\mathrm{d}S=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\lim_{r\to\infty}\int_{S_{r}}\log q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\,\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\cdot\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y}_{t})\,\mathrm{d}S=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle:=\lim_{r\to\infty}\int_{S_{r}}\frac{1}{2}\,\frac{p(\mathbf{y}_{t})}{q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})}\,\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\cdot\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y}_{t})\,\mathrm{d}S=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle:=\lim_{r\to\infty}\int_{S_{r}}\frac{1}{2}\,\frac{p(\mathbf{y}_{t})}{q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})}\,\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\cdot\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y}_{t})\,\mathrm{d}S=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, note that the limits <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> obviously exist, as each of these limits can be expressed as the sum of two converging integrals.
We prove (<a href="#A1.E34" title="In Lemma 2 (Vanishing boundary flux). ‣ A.4 Lemmas ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>); the argument for (<a href="#A1.E35" title="In Lemma 2 (Vanishing boundary flux). ‣ A.4 Lemmas ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>) is analogous.
For brevity, omit the subscript <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and write <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math> to be unit vector normal to <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> at the point <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under this notation <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d{\mathbf{s_{r}}}=||d{\mathbf{s_{r}}}||\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝐫</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝐫</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d{\mathbf{s_{r}}}=||d{\mathbf{s_{r}}}||\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math>. We integrate over <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> the surface integral in (<a href="#A1.E34" title="In Lemma 2 (Vanishing boundary flux). ‣ A.4 Lemmas ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>) and apply Green’s identity to find the relations. Set</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f(r):=\int_{S_{r}}\log q(\mathbf{y})\,\nabla p(\mathbf{y})\cdot d{\mathbf{s_{r}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝐫</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(r):=\int_{S_{r}}\log q(\mathbf{y})\,\nabla p(\mathbf{y})\cdot d{\mathbf{s_{r}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">By the coarea formula (spherical coordinates),</span></p>
<table id="A1.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{\infty}f(r)\,\mathrm{d}r=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\nabla p(\mathbf{y})\cdot\left(\log q(\mathbf{y})\,\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})\right)\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{\infty}f(r)\,\mathrm{d}r=\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\nabla p(\mathbf{y})\cdot\left(\log q(\mathbf{y})\,\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})\right)\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">Using the product rule and the divergence theorem on <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{B_{r}}\nabla p(\mathbf{y})\cdot\big(\log q(\mathbf{y})\,\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})\big)\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{B_{r}}\nabla p(\mathbf{y})\cdot\big(\log q(\mathbf{y})\,\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})\big)\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{r\rightarrow\infty}\int_{S_{r}}p(\mathbf{y})\log q(\mathbf{y})\,\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})\cdot d\mathbf{s_{r}}\;-\;\int_{B_{r}}p(\mathbf{y})\,\nabla\!\cdot\!\big(\log q(\mathbf{y})\,\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})\big)\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝐬</mi><mi>𝐫</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mpadded style="width:0.663em;" width="0.663em"><mo>∇</mo></mpadded><mo rspace="0.052em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{r\rightarrow\infty}\int_{S_{r}}p(\mathbf{y})\log q(\mathbf{y})\,\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})\cdot d\mathbf{s_{r}}\;-\;\int_{B_{r}}p(\mathbf{y})\,\nabla\!\cdot\!\big(\log q(\mathbf{y})\,\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})\big)\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">Letting <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> we bound the two terms on the right-hand side.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">First term.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By the coarea formula,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{r}^{\infty}\int_{S_{r}}\big|p(\mathbf{y})\log q(\mathbf{y})\big|\,\mathrm{d}S\,\mathrm{d}r=\int_{\|\mathbf{y}\|&gt;r}\big|p(\mathbf{y})\log q(\mathbf{y})\big|\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}\xrightarrow[r\to\infty]{}0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">∫</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">r</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mphantom></mphantom></munderover><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{r}^{\infty}\int_{S_{r}}\big|p(\mathbf{y})\log q(\mathbf{y})\big|\,\mathrm{d}S\,\mathrm{d}r=\int_{\|\mathbf{y}\|&gt;r}\big|p(\mathbf{y})\log q(\mathbf{y})\big|\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}\xrightarrow[r\to\infty]{}0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">because <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{p}[|\log q(\mathbf{y})|]&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{p}[|\log q(\mathbf{y})|]&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{S_{r}}p(\mathbf{y})\log q(\mathbf{y})\,\mathrm{d}S\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{S_{r}}p(\mathbf{y})\log q(\mathbf{y})\,\mathrm{d}S\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> along the full sequence <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g., via a Cesàro argument).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Second term.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now we note that the absolute value of the divergence in the second term satisfies the relation</p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left|\nabla\cdot\left(\log q(\mathbf{y})\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})\right)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left|\nabla\cdot\left(\log q(\mathbf{y})\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})\right)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\left|\nabla q(\mathbf{y})\cdot\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})\right|}{q(\mathbf{y})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\left|\nabla q(\mathbf{y})\cdot\mathbf{e}_{S_{r}}(\mathbf{y})\right|}{q(\mathbf{y})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\left\|\nabla q(\mathbf{y})\right\|}{q(\mathbf{y})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\left\|\nabla q(\mathbf{y})\right\|}{q(\mathbf{y})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Hence, we have</p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\|\nabla q(\mathbf{y})\|}{q(\mathbf{y})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\|\nabla q(\mathbf{y})\|}{q(\mathbf{y})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left[\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\frac{q(\mathbf{x})}{q(\mathbf{y})}(2\pi\sigma^{2}_{t})^{-\frac{D}{2}}\bigl(\frac{\|y_{i}-\alpha_{t}x_{i}\|}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\bigr)\exp\!\ \bigl(-\frac{\|\mathbf{y}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\mathbf{x}\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\bigr)\,d\mathbf{x}.\right]^{2}\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left[\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\frac{q(\mathbf{x})}{q(\mathbf{y})}(2\pi\sigma^{2}_{t})^{-\frac{D}{2}}\bigl(\frac{\|y_{i}-\alpha_{t}x_{i}\|}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\bigr)\exp\!\ \bigl(-\frac{\|\mathbf{y}_{t}-\alpha_{t}\mathbf{x}\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\bigr)\,d\mathbf{x}.\right]^{2}\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left[\mathbb{E}\left(\frac{Y_{i}-\alpha_{t}X_{i}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\Big|\mathbf{Y}=\mathbf{y}\right)\right]^{2}\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left[\mathbb{E}\left(\frac{Y_{i}-\alpha_{t}X_{i}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\Big|\mathbf{Y}=\mathbf{y}\right)\right]^{2}\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left(\mathbb{E}\left(\left(\frac{Y_{i}-\alpha_{t}X_{i}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right)^{2}\Big|\mathbf{Y}=\mathbf{y}\right)\right)\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(\sum_{i=1}^{n}\left(\mathbb{E}\left(\left(\frac{Y_{i}-\alpha_{t}X_{i}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right)^{2}\Big|\mathbf{Y}=\mathbf{y}\right)\right)\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\mathbb{E}\left(\left(\frac{\|\mathbf{Y}-\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}\|}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right)^{2}\Big|\mathbf{Y}=\mathbf{y}\right)\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\mathbb{E}\left(\left(\frac{\|\mathbf{Y}-\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}\|}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right)^{2}\Big|\mathbf{Y}=\mathbf{y}\right)\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Integrating w.r.t. <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{y})\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{y})\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math> and applying Jensen, we can write the chain of inequalities</p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}^{n}}p(\mathbf{y})\frac{\|\nabla q(\mathbf{y})\|}{q(\mathbf{y})}d\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}^{n}}p(\mathbf{y})\frac{\|\nabla q(\mathbf{y})\|}{q(\mathbf{y})}d\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{p}\left\{\left(\mathbb{E}\left(\left(\frac{\|\mathbf{Y}-\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}\|}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right)^{2}\Big|\mathbf{Y}=\mathbf{y}\right)\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}_{p}\left\{\left(\mathbb{E}\left(\left(\frac{\|\mathbf{Y}-\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}\|}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right)^{2}\Big|\mathbf{Y}=\mathbf{y}\right)\right)^{\frac{1}{2}}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left\{\mathbb{E}_{p}\left(\mathbb{E}\left(\left(\frac{\|\mathbf{Y}-\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}\|}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right)^{2}\Big|\mathbf{Y}=\mathbf{y}\right)\right)\right\}^{\frac{1}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝐘</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left\{\mathbb{E}_{p}\left(\mathbb{E}\left(\left(\frac{\|\mathbf{Y}-\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}\|}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right)^{2}\Big|\mathbf{Y}=\mathbf{y}\right)\right)\right\}^{\frac{1}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left[\mathbb{E}_{p}\left(\left(\frac{\|\mathbf{N}\|}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right)^{2}\right)\right]^{\frac{1}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐍</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left[\mathbb{E}_{p}\left(\left(\frac{\|\mathbf{N}\|}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\right)^{2}\right)\right]^{\frac{1}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\infty," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\infty,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">which means that</p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{p}\big[\|\nabla\log q(\mathbf{y})\|\big]\leq\Big(\mathbb{E}_{p}\big[\|\mathbf{N}\|^{2}/\sigma_{t}^{4}\big]\Big)^{1/2}&lt;\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐍</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{p}\big[\|\nabla\log q(\mathbf{y})\|\big]\leq\Big(\mathbb{E}_{p}\big[\|\mathbf{N}\|^{2}/\sigma_{t}^{4}\big]\Big)^{1/2}&lt;\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Therefore the right-hand side of (<a href="#A1.E37" title="In Proof. ‣ A.4 Lemmas ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>) is finite, so</p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{\infty}f(r)\,\mathrm{d}r&lt;\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{\infty}f(r)\,\mathrm{d}r&lt;\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is locally absolutely continuous in <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> (by the smoothness of <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> and the coarea formula), hence <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{r\to\infty}f(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{r\to\infty}f(r)</annotation></semantics></math> exists. Since <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{\infty}f(r)\,\mathrm{d}r&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{\infty}f(r)\,\mathrm{d}r&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, this limit must equal <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. The proof of <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math> follows by the same steps with <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tfrac{1}{2}\,\frac{p}{q}\nabla q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{1}{2}\,\frac{p}{q}\nabla q</annotation></semantics></math> in place of <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log q\,\nabla p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log q\,\nabla p</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> and consider the Gaussian channel in (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2.1 Incremental Gaussian Channel and Maximum Likelihood Estimation ‣ 2 Background ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).
Let <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{y}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{y}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝛉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> be the output densities induced by inputs <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\mathbf{x};\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝛉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\mathbf{x};\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
Assume <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\cdot;\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝛉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\cdot;\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> are sufficiently smooth and integrable so that differentiation under the integral sign is justified and the boundary terms in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Vanishing boundary flux). ‣ A.4 Lemmas ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> vanish.
Then the derivative of the mismatched output cross-entropy</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{H}\big(p(\mathbf{y}_{t}),q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\big):=-\!\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\,\log q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}_{t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.026em">−</mo><msub><mo lspace="0.026em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}\big(p(\mathbf{y}_{t}),q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\big):=-\!\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\,\log q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with respect to the noise variance <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A1.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}\sigma_{t}^{2}}\,\mathcal{H}\big(p(\mathbf{y}_{t}),q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\big)=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\left(\frac{\nabla q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\cdot\nabla p(\mathbf{y}_{t})}{q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})}\;+\;\nabla\!\left(\frac{p(\mathbf{y}_{t})}{q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})}\right)\cdot\nabla q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\right)\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.663em;" width="0.663em"><mo>∇</mo></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}\sigma_{t}^{2}}\,\mathcal{H}\big(p(\mathbf{y}_{t}),q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\big)=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\left(\frac{\nabla q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\cdot\nabla p(\mathbf{y}_{t})}{q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})}\;+\;\nabla\!\left(\frac{p(\mathbf{y}_{t})}{q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})}\right)\cdot\nabla q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\right)\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{a}\cdot\mathbf{b}=\langle\mathbf{a},\mathbf{b}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐚</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐛</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐛</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{a}\cdot\mathbf{b}=\langle\mathbf{a},\mathbf{b}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Euclidean inner product.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition of cross-entropy in Def. <a href="#Thmdefinition4" title="Definition 4. ‣ A.2 Definitions ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{H}\big(p(\mathbf{y}_{t}),q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\big)=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\,\log q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}_{t}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}\big(p(\mathbf{y}_{t}),q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\big)=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\,\log q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Differentiating w.r.t. <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (justified by the assumed regularity) yields</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}\sigma_{t}^{2}}\Big(-\!\int p\log q\Big)=-\int\log q\,\frac{\partial p}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}_{t}\;-\;\int p\,\frac{\partial}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}\log q\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}_{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}\sigma_{t}^{2}}\Big(-\!\int p\log q\Big)=-\int\log q\,\frac{\partial p}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}_{t}\;-\;\int p\,\frac{\partial}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}\log q\,\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we abbreviate <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=p(\mathbf{y}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=p(\mathbf{y}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under Gaussian smoothing (heat equation),</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial p}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}=\frac{1}{2}\,\Delta_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}p,\qquad\frac{\partial q}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}=\frac{1}{2}\,\Delta_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}q,\qquad\frac{\partial}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}\log q=\frac{1}{q}\frac{\partial q}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}=\frac{1}{2}\,\frac{\Delta_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}q}{q}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mi>q</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial p}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}=\frac{1}{2}\,\Delta_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}p,\qquad\frac{\partial q}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}=\frac{1}{2}\,\Delta_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}q,\qquad\frac{\partial}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}\log q=\frac{1}{q}\frac{\partial q}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}=\frac{1}{2}\,\frac{\Delta_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}q}{q}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">We now recall Green’s identity: If <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\phi}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\phi}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝝍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> are twice continuously differentiable functions in <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> is any set bounded by a piecewise smooth, closed, oriented surface <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\int_{V}\boldsymbol{\phi}\nabla^{2}\boldsymbol{\psi}\,dV=\int_{S}\boldsymbol{\phi}\nabla\boldsymbol{\psi}\cdot d\mathbf{s}-\int_{V}\nabla\boldsymbol{\phi}\cdot\nabla\boldsymbol{\psi}\,dV," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>V</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>V</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>S</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐬</mi><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo>∫</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>V</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{V}\boldsymbol{\phi}\nabla^{2}\boldsymbol{\psi}\,dV=\int_{S}\boldsymbol{\phi}\nabla\boldsymbol{\psi}\cdot d\mathbf{s}-\int_{V}\nabla\boldsymbol{\phi}\cdot\nabla\boldsymbol{\psi}\,dV,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\boldsymbol{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\boldsymbol{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the gradient of <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{s}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the elementary area vector, and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\boldsymbol{\phi}\cdot d\mathbf{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\boldsymbol{\phi}\cdot d\mathbf{s}</annotation></semantics></math> is the inner product of these two vectors. This identity plays the role of integration by parts in <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">To apply Green’s identity to (<a href="#A1.E42" title="In Proof. ‣ Second term. ‣ A.4 Lemmas ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>), we let <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> be the <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>-sphere of radius <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> centered at the origin and having surface <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we use Green’s identity on <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\phi}(\mathbf{y}_{t})=\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\phi}(\mathbf{y}_{t})=\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{y}_{t})=p(\mathbf{y}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝝍</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\psi}(\mathbf{y}_{t})=p(\mathbf{y}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and take the limit as <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. In Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Vanishing boundary flux). ‣ A.4 Lemmas ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> the surface integral over <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is shown to vanish in the limit. Hence, by applying heat equation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite> and Green’s identity for the first term on right hide side, we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\int\log q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\,d\mathbf{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\int\log q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\,d\mathbf{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E44.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{2}\int\log q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\Delta_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\,d\mathbf{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{2}\int\log q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\Delta_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\,d\mathbf{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\int\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\cdot\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\,d\mathbf{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\int\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\cdot\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\,d\mathbf{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\frac{\nabla q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\cdot\nabla p(\mathbf{y}_{t})}{q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})}\,d\mathbf{y}_{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\frac{\nabla q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\cdot\nabla p(\mathbf{y}_{t})}{q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})}\,d\mathbf{y}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where we used integration by parts in high dimension and the vanishing boundary terms from Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma2" title="Lemma 2 (Vanishing boundary flux). ‣ A.4 Lemmas ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. For the second term,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E47.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\int p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}\log q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\,d\mathbf{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\int p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}\log q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\,d\mathbf{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E47.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\int p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\frac{\nabla_{\sigma_{t}^{2}}q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})}{q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})}\,d\mathbf{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msub><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\int p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\frac{\nabla_{\sigma_{t}^{2}}q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})}{q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})}\,d\mathbf{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E48.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{2}\int\left(\frac{p(\mathbf{y}_{t})}{q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})}\right)\Delta_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\,d\mathbf{y}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{2}\int\left(\frac{p(\mathbf{y}_{t})}{q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})}\right)\Delta_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\,d\mathbf{y}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\nabla\left(\frac{p(\mathbf{y}_{t})}{q(\mathbf{y}_{t})}\right)\cdot\nabla q(\mathbf{y}_{t})\,d\mathbf{y}_{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\nabla\left(\frac{p(\mathbf{y}_{t})}{q(\mathbf{y}_{t})}\right)\cdot\nabla q(\mathbf{y}_{t})\,d\mathbf{y}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">where we again applied Green’s identity and used the vanishing of the boundary flux.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Summing the two contributions yields (<a href="#A1.E41" title="In Lemma 3. ‣ Second term. ‣ A.4 Lemmas ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X,\mathcal{S},\mu_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X,\mathcal{S},\mu_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> be probability spaces, and let <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T:X\to Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T:X\to Y</annotation></semantics></math> be a measurable transformation inducing probability measures <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Y,\mathcal{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Y,\mathcal{T})</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nu_{i}(G)=\mu_{i}(T^{-1}(G)),\quad\forall G\in\mathcal{T},\quad i=1,2." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{i}(G)=\mu_{i}(T^{-1}(G)),\quad\forall G\in\mathcal{T},\quad i=1,2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Denote the Radon-Nikodym derivatives of <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to a common reference measure <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}(y)=\frac{d\nu_{i}}{d\gamma}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}(y)=\frac{d\nu_{i}}{d\gamma}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, the KL divergence remains invariant under the transformation <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\nu_{1}||\nu_{2})=D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mu_{1}||\mu_{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\nu_{1}||\nu_{2})=D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mu_{1}||\mu_{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\nu_{1}||\nu_{2})=\int_{Y}g_{1}(y)\log\frac{g_{1}(y)}{g_{2}(y)}d\gamma(y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>Y</mi></msub><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\nu_{1}||\nu_{2})=\int_{Y}g_{1}(y)\log\frac{g_{1}(y)}{g_{2}(y)}d\gamma(y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> be a reference measure on <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> has densities <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{i}(x)=\frac{d\mu_{i}}{d\lambda}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{i}(x)=\frac{d\mu_{i}}{d\lambda}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">By the change of variables under <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, the density functions transform as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}(y)=\frac{d\nu_{i}}{d\gamma}(y)=\frac{d\mu_{i}}{d\lambda}(T^{-1}(y))J_{T}^{-1}(y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}(y)=\frac{d\nu_{i}}{d\gamma}(y)=\frac{d\mu_{i}}{d\lambda}(T^{-1}(y))J_{T}^{-1}(y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{T}(y)=\left|\det\frac{dT}{dx}\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{T}(y)=\left|\det\frac{dT}{dx}\right|</annotation></semantics></math> is the Jacobian determinant of <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting into the definition of KL divergence:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\nu_{1}||\nu_{2})=\int_{Y}g_{1}(y)\log\frac{g_{1}(y)}{g_{2}(y)}d\gamma(y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>Y</mi></msub><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\nu_{1}||\nu_{2})=\int_{Y}g_{1}(y)\log\frac{g_{1}(y)}{g_{2}(y)}d\gamma(y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">we expand:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\int_{Y}\left(f_{1}(T^{-1}(y))J_{T}^{-1}\right)\log\frac{f_{1}(T^{-1}(y))J_{T}^{-1}}{f_{2}(T^{-1}(y))J_{T}^{-1}}d\gamma(y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mi>Y</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>J</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\int_{Y}\left(f_{1}(T^{-1}(y))J_{T}^{-1}\right)\log\frac{f_{1}(T^{-1}(y))J_{T}^{-1}}{f_{2}(T^{-1}(y))J_{T}^{-1}}d\gamma(y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since the Jacobian terms cancel, we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=\int_{Y}f_{1}(T^{-1}(y))\log\frac{f_{1}(T^{-1}(y))}{f_{2}(T^{-1}(y))}d\gamma(y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>Y</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\int_{Y}f_{1}(T^{-1}(y))\log\frac{f_{1}(T^{-1}(y))}{f_{2}(T^{-1}(y))}d\gamma(y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p11.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p11.4.1" class="ltx_text">By the change of variables <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=T^{-1}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=T^{-1}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>, we rewrite this as:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="=\int_{X}f_{1}(z)\log\frac{f_{1}(z)}{f_{2}(z)}d\lambda(z)=D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mu_{1}||\mu_{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>X</mi></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=\int_{X}f_{1}(z)\log\frac{f_{1}(z)}{f_{2}(z)}d\lambda(z)=D_{\mathrm{KL}}(\mu_{1}||\mu_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p11.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p11.5.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, the KL divergence is invariant under the transformation <math id="A1.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, completing the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Proof and Remark of Theorems</h3>

<section id="A1.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.5.1 </span>Proof of Theorem. <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Score Matching as the Small-Noise Limit of KL Divergence). ‣ 3.1 Relationship between Score Matching and KL Divergence ‣ 3 Variance-Aware Likelihood Estimation of Diffusion models ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h4>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem  <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Score Matching as the Small-Noise Limit of KL Divergence). ‣ 3.1 Relationship between Score Matching and KL Divergence ‣ 3 Variance-Aware Likelihood Estimation of Diffusion models ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</span> <span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}\sim p(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}\sim p(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> be an arbitrary distributed random vector on <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝛉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> be a parametric model with <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{X}}\sim q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝛉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{X}}\sim q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the perturbed observation</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{X}}:=\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}+\sigma_{t}\boldsymbol{\Psi}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚿</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{X}}:=\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}+\sigma_{t}\boldsymbol{\Psi},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Psi}</annotation></semantics></math> is a random vector independent of <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math> , satisfying <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\boldsymbol{\Psi}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝚿</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\boldsymbol{\Psi}]=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Cov}(\boldsymbol{\Psi})=\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Cov}(\boldsymbol{\Psi})=\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\sigma_{t}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\sigma_{t}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\sigma_{t}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\sigma_{t}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the densities of <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{X}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{X}}</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> with noise variance <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. Suppose that the KL divergence <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p_{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\|q_{\sigma_{t}^{2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p_{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\|q_{\sigma_{t}^{2}})</annotation></semantics></math> is finite for sufficiently small <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then the following limit holds:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E50.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left.\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p_{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\|q_{\sigma_{t}^{2}})\right|_{\sigma_{t}^{2}\to 0^{+}}=-\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p(\mathbf{x})\left\|\nabla\log p(\mathbf{x})-\nabla\log q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})\right\|^{2}d\mathbf{x}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left.\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p_{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\|q_{\sigma_{t}^{2}})\right|_{\sigma_{t}^{2}\to 0^{+}}=-\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p(\mathbf{x})\left\|\nabla\log p(\mathbf{x})-\nabla\log q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})\right\|^{2}d\mathbf{x},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left.\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\|q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta}))\right|_{\sigma_{t}^{2}\to 0^{+}}=-\frac{1}{2}I\left(p(\mathbf{x})\|q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left.\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}D_{\mathrm{KL}}(p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\|q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta}))\right|_{\sigma_{t}^{2}\to 0^{+}}=-\frac{1}{2}I\left(p(\mathbf{x})\|q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I(\cdot\|\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(\cdot\|\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Fisher divergence (equivalently, score matching objective) between <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">According to the definition of relative entropy (See Def. <a href="#Thmdefinition3" title="Definition 3. ‣ A.2 Definitions ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E51.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}D_{\text{KL}}(p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\|q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))=\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\log(\frac{p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})}{q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})})\,d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}D_{\text{KL}}(p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\|q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))=\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\log(\frac{p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})}{q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})})\,d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\frac{\partial p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}\log(\frac{p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})}{q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})})+p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\frac{\partial}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}\log(\frac{p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})}{q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})})\,d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\frac{\partial p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}\log(\frac{p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})}{q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})})+p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\frac{\partial}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}\log(\frac{p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})}{q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})})\,d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\frac{\partial p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}\log(\frac{p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})}{q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})})+p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\left(\frac{\partial p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}/p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})-\frac{\partial q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}/q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})\right)\,d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\frac{\partial p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}\log(\frac{p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})}{q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})})+p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\left(\frac{\partial p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}/p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})-\frac{\partial q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})}{\partial\sigma_{t}^{2}}/q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})\right)\,d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Invoking Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ A.4 Lemmas ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> on (<a href="#A1.E53" title="In Proof. ‣ A.5.1 Proof of Theorem. ‣ A.5 Proof and Remark of Theorems ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">53</span></a>) yields</span></p>
<table id="A1.E54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E54.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}D_{\text{KL}}(p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\|q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta}))\bigg|_{\sigma_{t}^{2}=0^{+}}=\frac{1}{2}\int\left(p^{\prime\prime}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\log(\frac{p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})}{q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})})+p^{\prime\prime}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})-\frac{q^{\prime\prime}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})}{q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})}\right)\,d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}D_{\text{KL}}(p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\|q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta}))\bigg|_{\sigma_{t}^{2}=0^{+}}=\frac{1}{2}\int\left(p^{\prime\prime}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\log(\frac{p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})}{q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})})+p^{\prime\prime}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})-\frac{q^{\prime\prime}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})}{q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})}\right)\,d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">For convenience, define:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\upsilon(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})=\log\frac{p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})}{q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})}=\log p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})-\log q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>υ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\upsilon(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})=\log\frac{p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})}{q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})}=\log p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})-\log q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Recall the Green’s identity:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\nu\nabla^{2}\mu\ d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}=\int_{\partial\mathbb{R}^{D}}\nu\frac{\partial\mu}{\partial n}dS-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\left(\nabla\nu\cdot\nabla\mu\right)\,d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\nu\nabla^{2}\mu\ d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}=\int_{\partial\mathbb{R}^{D}}\nu\frac{\partial\mu}{\partial n}dS-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\left(\nabla\nu\cdot\nabla\mu\right)\,d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Setting <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu=p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu=p</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu=\upsilon=\log\frac{p}{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>υ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu=\upsilon=\log\frac{p}{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p^{\prime\prime}\upsilon\ \,d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}=\int_{\partial\mathbb{R}^{D}}p\frac{\partial\upsilon}{\partial n}dS-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\left(\nabla\upsilon\cdot\nabla p\right)\ d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>υ</mi><mo lspace="0.670em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>υ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>υ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p^{\prime\prime}\upsilon\ \,d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}=\int_{\partial\mathbb{R}^{D}}p\frac{\partial\upsilon}{\partial n}dS-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\left(\nabla\upsilon\cdot\nabla p\right)\ d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> has finite differential Shannon entropy, the boundary integral vanishes, leaving</span></p>
<table id="A1.E57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E57.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p^{\prime\prime}\upsilon\ d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\left(\nabla\upsilon\cdot\nabla p\right)\ d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mi>υ</mi><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>υ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi><mo rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p^{\prime\prime}\upsilon\ d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\left(\nabla\upsilon\cdot\nabla p\right)\ d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">For the term <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime\prime}p/q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime\prime}p/q</annotation></semantics></math>, we apply the same identity:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E58.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\frac{q^{\prime\prime}p}{q}d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\left(p\nabla\log q\cdot\nabla\log q\right)\ d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\frac{q^{\prime\prime}p}{q}d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\left(p\nabla\log q\cdot\nabla\log q\right)\ d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.8.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p^{\prime\prime}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p^{\prime\prime}(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}=0</annotation></semantics></math> under appropriate boundary conditions, it does not contribute. Similar technique was used in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>, <a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">58</a>, <a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite>.
Using <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\upsilon=\log p-\log q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>υ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\upsilon=\log p-\log q</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\upsilon=\nabla\log p-\nabla\log q." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>υ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\upsilon=\nabla\log p-\nabla\log q.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.9.1" class="ltx_text">Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla p\cdot\nabla\upsilon=\nabla p\cdot(\nabla\log p-\nabla\log q)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>υ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla p\cdot\nabla\upsilon=\nabla p\cdot(\nabla\log p-\nabla\log q).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.10.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla p=p\nabla\log p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla p=p\nabla\log p</annotation></semantics></math>, we substitute:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E61.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla p\cdot\nabla\upsilon=p\nabla\log p\cdot(\nabla\log p-\nabla\log q)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>υ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla p\cdot\nabla\upsilon=p\nabla\log p\cdot(\nabla\log p-\nabla\log q).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.11.1" class="ltx_text">Expanding,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\log p\cdot(\nabla\log p-\nabla\log q)=\|\nabla\log p\|^{2}-\nabla\log p\cdot\nabla\log q." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\log p\cdot(\nabla\log p-\nabla\log q)=\|\nabla\log p\|^{2}-\nabla\log p\cdot\nabla\log q.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.12.1" class="ltx_text">Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E63.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p^{\prime\prime}\upsilon\,d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p\left(\|\nabla\log p\|^{2}-\nabla\log p\cdot\nabla\log q\right)d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mi>υ</mi><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p^{\prime\prime}\upsilon\,d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p\left(\|\nabla\log p\|^{2}-\nabla\log p\cdot\nabla\log q\right)d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.13.1" class="ltx_text">Using the result for <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{\prime\prime}p/q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{\prime\prime}p/q</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E64.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\frac{q^{\prime\prime}p}{q}d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\left(p\nabla\log q\cdot\nabla\log q\,\right)d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\frac{q^{\prime\prime}p}{q}d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\left(p\nabla\log q\cdot\nabla\log q\,\right)d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.14.1" class="ltx_text">Summing both contributions,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E65.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\left(-p\left(\|\nabla\log p\|^{2}-\nabla\log p\cdot\nabla\log q\right)-p\|\nabla\log q\|^{2}+p\nabla\log p\cdot\nabla\log q\right)\,d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\left(-p\left(\|\nabla\log p\|^{2}-\nabla\log p\cdot\nabla\log q\right)-p\|\nabla\log q\|^{2}+p\nabla\log p\cdot\nabla\log q\right)\,d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.15.1" class="ltx_text">Rearranging, we conclude:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E66.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}D_{\text{KL}}(p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\|q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta}))\bigg|_{\sigma_{t}^{2}=0^{+}}=-\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p(\mathbf{x})\|\nabla\log p(\mathbf{x})-\nabla\log q(\mathbf{x};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\|_{2}^{2}\,d\mathbf{x}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}D_{\text{KL}}(p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\|q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta}))\bigg|_{\sigma_{t}^{2}=0^{+}}=-\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p(\mathbf{x})\|\nabla\log p(\mathbf{x})-\nabla\log q(\mathbf{x};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\|_{2}^{2}\,d\mathbf{x},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p2.16.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to the classical result in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>, <a href="#bib.bib78" title="" class="ltx_ref">78</a>]</cite>, the relation in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Score Matching as the Small-Noise Limit of KL Divergence). ‣ 3.1 Relationship between Score Matching and KL Divergence ‣ 3 Variance-Aware Likelihood Estimation of Diffusion models ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> holds because both sides quantify the error induced by a mismatch between the true distribution <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and the prior <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> provided to the estimator. Naturally, when <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=q</annotation></semantics></math>, both sides vanish; otherwise, the derivative is strictly negative, indicating that perturbations reduce the relative entropy. This observation also yields the relative entropy version of the data processing inequality:</p>
<table id="A1.E67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E67.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\text{KL}}(\rho\|\nu)\geq D_{\text{KL}}(\bar{\rho}\|\bar{\nu})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{KL}}(\rho\|\nu)\geq D_{\text{KL}}(\bar{\rho}\|\bar{\nu}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A1.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\rho}=\int W(\mathbf{y}|\mathbf{x})\,d\rho(\mathbf{x}),\qquad\bar{\nu}=\int W(\mathbf{y}|\mathbf{x})\,d\nu(\mathbf{x})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\rho}=\int W(\mathbf{y}|\mathbf{x})\,d\rho(\mathbf{x}),\qquad\bar{\nu}=\int W(\mathbf{y}|\mathbf{x})\,d\nu(\mathbf{x}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a noisy channel. This inequality asserts that the KL divergence between two distributions decreases under the action of a common channel, which is consistent with the data processing argument used in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>]</cite>, where, the channel <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to time-reversed Brownian motion, which can be viewed as a continuous analogue of the Gaussian channel <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib82" title="" class="ltx_ref">82</a>]</cite>. Under the assumption that <math id="A1.SS5.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\rho}(\mathbf{x})=\bar{\nu}(\mathbf{x})=\pi(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ν</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\rho}(\mathbf{x})=\bar{\nu}(\mathbf{x})=\pi(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>, the result further implies that the diffusion process smooths the discrepancy between inputs. Moreover, the neural network acts as a channel simulator, enabling efficient sampling by integrating its output into the neural ODE solvers <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.5.2 </span>Proof of Proposition. <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Thermodynamic Decomposition of Mismatched Entropy). ‣ 3.2 Bounding the Mismatched Entropy with Thermodynamic Diffusion ‣ 3 Variance-Aware Likelihood Estimation of Diffusion models ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></h4>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Thermodynamic Decomposition of Mismatched Entropy). ‣ 3.2 Bounding the Mismatched Entropy with Thermodynamic Diffusion ‣ 3 Variance-Aware Likelihood Estimation of Diffusion models ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</span> <span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the signal model (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2.1 Incremental Gaussian Channel and Maximum Likelihood Estimation ‣ 2 Background ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), suppose <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝛉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\tilde{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})</annotation></semantics></math> have continuous second-order derivatives and finite second moments. Denote by <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{y}_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{y}_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> the output signals of channel at time <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> when inputs are <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝛉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. Assume <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(\mathbf{x})=\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\mathbf{x})=\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>, which is independent of <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝛉</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the channel (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2.1 Incremental Gaussian Channel and Maximum Likelihood Estimation ‣ 2 Background ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) for any <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, then for arbitrary datapoint <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and small <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{0}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{0}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\sigma_{0}^{2}\ll 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≪</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\sigma_{0}^{2}\ll 1</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{x}),q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))=\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}),\pi(\mathbf{x}))+\mathcal{J}_{\text{DSM}}(\boldsymbol{\theta};\sigma_{t}^{2}(\cdot))-\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})\|^{2}d\sigma^{2}_{t}+o(\sigma_{0}^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>DSM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{x}),q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))=\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}),\pi(\mathbf{x}))+\mathcal{J}_{\text{DSM}}(\boldsymbol{\theta};\sigma_{t}^{2}(\cdot))-\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})\|^{2}d\sigma^{2}_{t}+o(\sigma_{0}^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Here, the denoising score matching objective is defined as</span></p>
<table id="A1.E69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{\text{DSM}}(\boldsymbol{\theta};\sigma^{2}(\cdot)):=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})-\hat{\boldsymbol{s}}(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\|_{2}^{2}\,d\sigma^{2}_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">DSM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{\text{DSM}}(\boldsymbol{\theta};\sigma^{2}(\cdot)):=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})-\hat{\boldsymbol{s}}(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\|_{2}^{2}\,d\sigma^{2}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{\boldsymbol{s}}(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})=\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta}):=-\hat{\mathbf{n}}(\mathbf{y}_{t},\eta_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})/\sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝛉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝛉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝛉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\boldsymbol{s}}(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})=\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log q(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta}):=-\hat{\mathbf{n}}(\mathbf{y}_{t},\eta_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})/\sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is a score network estimator.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall the thermodynamic integration commonly used in statistical physics:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{\Xi}\frac{d}{d\xi}f(\xi)d\xi=f(\Xi)-f(0)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{\Xi}\frac{d}{d\xi}f(\xi)d\xi=f(\Xi)-f(0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f(\sigma_{t}^{2}):=D_{\text{KL}}\bigl(p(\mathbf{y})\|q(\mathbf{y};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\sigma_{t}^{2}):=D_{\text{KL}}\bigl(p(\mathbf{y})\|q(\mathbf{y};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Y}_{t}=\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}+\sigma_{t}\mathbf{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐘</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐍</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Y}_{t}=\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}+\sigma_{t}\mathbf{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{\Xi}\frac{d}{d\xi}f(\xi)d\xi=f(\Xi)-f(0)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{\Xi}\frac{d}{d\xi}f(\xi)d\xi=f(\Xi)-f(0),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">becomes equivalent to</span></p>
<table id="A1.E72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}f(\sigma_{t}^{2})d\sigma_{t}^{2}=f(\sigma_{1}^{2})-f(0)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}f(\sigma_{t}^{2})d\sigma_{t}^{2}=f(\sigma_{1}^{2})-f(0),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">which yields the following expression,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E73.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\int_{0}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{y})\|q(\mathbf{y};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))=D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1})\|q(\mathbf{y}_{1};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))-D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{x})\|q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{y})\|q(\mathbf{y};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))=D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1})\|q(\mathbf{y}_{1};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))-D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{x})\|q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">This occurs because the KL divergence remains invariant under measurable transformations shown in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ Second term. ‣ A.4 Lemmas ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. In particular, probability density transformation serves as an illustrative example. Let <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}\sim\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}\sim\rho</annotation></semantics></math> be a random vector on the measure space with a probability density function <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>. We define the transformation <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}^{\prime}=T(\mathbf{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}^{\prime}=T(\mathbf{X})</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, the probability density function of <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted as <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{x}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{x}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, can be determined using:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E74" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{x}^{\prime})=p(T^{-1}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime}))\left|\frac{d}{d\mathbf{x}^{\prime}}T^{-1}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime})\right|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{x}^{\prime})=p(T^{-1}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime}))\left|\frac{d}{d\mathbf{x}^{\prime}}T^{-1}(\mathbf{x}^{\prime})\right|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Furthermore, the KL divergence satisfies the following property:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E75.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\text{KL}}(\rho(\alpha\mathbf{x})\|\nu(\alpha\mathbf{x}))=D_{\text{KL}}(\rho(\mathbf{x})\|\nu(\mathbf{x}))\quad\forall\alpha&gt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{KL}}(\rho(\alpha\mathbf{x})\|\nu(\alpha\mathbf{x}))=D_{\text{KL}}(\rho(\mathbf{x})\|\nu(\mathbf{x}))\quad\forall\alpha&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">which implies that the KL divergence depends solely on the relative shape of the two distributions rather than their absolute scale. Invoke the Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ Second term. ‣ A.4 Lemmas ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and results in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>]</cite> on (<a href="#A1.E73" title="In Proof. ‣ A.5.2 Proof of Proposition. ‣ A.5 Proof and Remark of Theorems ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">73</span></a>) yields</span></p>
<table id="A1.E76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E76.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{x})\|q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))=D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1})\|q(\mathbf{y}_{1};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))+\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}I(p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\|q(\mathbf{y}_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))d\sigma_{t}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{x})\|q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))=D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1})\|q(\mathbf{y}_{1};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))+\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}I(p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\|q(\mathbf{y}_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))d\sigma_{t}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">With the fact that <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\mathbf{y}_{1};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}):=\pi(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\mathbf{y}_{1};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}):=\pi(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>, which is independent of <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.E77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E77.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{x})\|q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))=D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1})\|\pi(\mathbf{x}))+\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}I(p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\|q(\mathbf{y}_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))\,d\sigma_{t}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{x})\|q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))=D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1})\|\pi(\mathbf{x}))+\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}I(p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\|q(\mathbf{y}_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))\,d\sigma_{t}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">The mismatched entropy between data and model becomes equivalent to</span></p>
<table id="A1.E78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E78.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{x}),q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))=D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{x})\|q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))+\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{x}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{x}),q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))=D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{x})\|q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))+\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{x})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(78)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Invoking (<a href="#A1.E77" title="In Proof. ‣ A.5.2 Proof of Proposition. ‣ A.5 Proof and Remark of Theorems ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">77</span></a>) on (<a href="#A1.E78" title="In Proof. ‣ A.5.2 Proof of Proposition. ‣ A.5 Proof and Remark of Theorems ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">78</span></a>) yields</span></p>
<table id="A1.E79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E79.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{x}),q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))=D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1})\|\pi(\mathbf{x}))+\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}I(p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\|q(\mathbf{y}_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))\,d\sigma_{t}^{2}+\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{x}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{x}),q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))=D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1})\|\pi(\mathbf{x}))+\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}I(p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\|q(\mathbf{y}_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))\,d\sigma_{t}^{2}+\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{x})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(79)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">Recall de Bruijin’s identity <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{t}))=\frac{1}{2}\mathcal{J}(p(\mathbf{y}_{t}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{t}))=\frac{1}{2}\mathcal{J}(p(\mathbf{y}_{t})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(80)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">Using thermodynamic integration again, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{0}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{t}))d\sigma_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{0}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{t}))d\sigma_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E81.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}))-\mathcal{H}(p(\alpha_{0}\mathbf{x}))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}))-\mathcal{H}(p(\alpha_{0}\mathbf{x})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(81)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.7.1" class="ltx_text">which is equivalent to</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{H}(p(\alpha_{0}\mathbf{x}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{H}(p(\alpha_{0}\mathbf{x}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E82.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}))-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\mathcal{J}(p(\mathbf{y}_{t}))d\sigma_{t}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}))-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\mathcal{J}(p(\mathbf{y}_{t}))d\sigma_{t}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.8.1" class="ltx_text">Recall the property of differential entropy (see Theorem 8.6.4 (8.71) in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>)</span></p>
<table id="A1.E83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}(a\mathbf{X})=\mathcal{H}(\mathbf{X})+\log|\det(a)|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(a\mathbf{X})=\mathcal{H}(\mathbf{X})+\log|\det(a)|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(83)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.9.1" class="ltx_text">and the connection with denoising score matching (see (11) in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib79" title="" class="ltx_ref">79</a>]</cite>)</span></p>
<table id="A1.E84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E84.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I(p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\|q(\mathbf{y}_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))=\mathbb{E}\left[\|\nabla\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})-\boldsymbol{s}(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\|^{2}\right]+\mathcal{J}(p(\mathbf{y}_{t}))-\mathbb{E}\left[\|\nabla\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})\|^{2}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I(p(\mathbf{y}_{t})\|q(\mathbf{y}_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))=\mathbb{E}\left[\|\nabla\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})-\boldsymbol{s}(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\|^{2}\right]+\mathcal{J}(p(\mathbf{y}_{t}))-\mathbb{E}\left[\|\nabla\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})\|^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(84)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.10.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle(p(\mathbf{x}),q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))=\Bigg(D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1})\|\pi(\mathbf{x}))+\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}))-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\mathcal{J}(p(\mathbf{y}_{t}))\,d\sigma_{t}^{2}-D\log|\alpha_{0}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup></mstyle><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi><mi>log</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(p(\mathbf{x}),q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))=\Bigg(D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1})\|\pi(\mathbf{x}))+\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}))-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\mathcal{J}(p(\mathbf{y}_{t}))\,d\sigma_{t}^{2}-D\log|\alpha_{0}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}\bigg(\int_{0}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[\|\nabla\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})-\hat{\boldsymbol{s}}(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\|^{2}\right]+\mathcal{J}(p(\mathbf{y}_{t}))-\mathbb{E}\left[\|\nabla\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})\|^{2}\right]d\sigma_{t}^{2}\bigg)\Bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}\bigg(\int_{0}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[\|\nabla\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})-\hat{\boldsymbol{s}}(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\|^{2}\right]+\mathcal{J}(p(\mathbf{y}_{t}))-\mathbb{E}\left[\|\nabla\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})\|^{2}\right]d\sigma_{t}^{2}\bigg)\Bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(85)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}),\pi(\mathbf{x}))+\mathcal{J}_{\text{DSM}}(\boldsymbol{\theta};\sigma_{t}^{2}(\cdot))-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})\|^{2}d\sigma^{2}_{t}-D\log|\alpha_{0}|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>DSM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}),\pi(\mathbf{x}))+\mathcal{J}_{\text{DSM}}(\boldsymbol{\theta};\sigma_{t}^{2}(\cdot))-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})\|^{2}d\sigma^{2}_{t}-D\log|\alpha_{0}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(86)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.11.1" class="ltx_text">Since the identity <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}+\alpha_{t}^{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}+\alpha_{t}^{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math> holds for all <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, setting the lower limit of integration such that <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{0}^{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{0}^{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{0}^{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{0}^{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\alpha_{0}|=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\alpha_{0}|=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus: <math id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log|\alpha_{0}|=\log 1=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log|\alpha_{0}|=\log 1=0</annotation></semantics></math>. And invoking Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Score Matching as the Small-Noise Limit of KL Divergence). ‣ 3.1 Relationship between Score Matching and KL Divergence ‣ 3 Variance-Aware Likelihood Estimation of Diffusion models ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we finally get</span></p>
<table id="A1.E87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{x}),q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))=\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}),\pi(\mathbf{x}))+\mathcal{J}_{\text{DSM}}(\boldsymbol{\theta};\sigma_{t}^{2}(\cdot))-\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})\|^{2}d\sigma^{2}_{t}+o(\sigma_{0}^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>DSM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{x}),q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}}))=\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}),\pi(\mathbf{x}))+\mathcal{J}_{\text{DSM}}(\boldsymbol{\theta};\sigma_{t}^{2}(\cdot))-\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\mathbb{E}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})\|^{2}d\sigma^{2}_{t}+o(\sigma_{0}^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(87)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.5.3 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 3.3 Bounding the log-likelihood on Individual Datapoints ‣ 3 Variance-Aware Likelihood Estimation of Diffusion models ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h4>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 3.3 Bounding the log-likelihood on Individual Datapoints ‣ 3 Variance-Aware Likelihood Estimation of Diffusion models ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</span> <span id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> Let <math id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})=\mathcal{N}(\alpha_{t}\mathbf{x},\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})=\mathcal{N}(\alpha_{t}\mathbf{x},\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the Gaussian channel at any time <math id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. With the same notations and conditions in Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Thermodynamic Decomposition of Mismatched Entropy). ‣ 3.2 Bounding the Mismatched Entropy with Thermodynamic Diffusion ‣ 3 Variance-Aware Likelihood Estimation of Diffusion models ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.E88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\log q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\leq\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}|\mathbf{x}),\mathbf{\pi}(\mathbf{x}))+\mathcal{L}_{\text{DSM}}(\sigma_{t}^{2};\boldsymbol{\theta})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DSM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\log q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\leq\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}|\mathbf{x}),\mathbf{\pi}(\mathbf{x}))+\mathcal{L}_{\text{DSM}}(\sigma_{t}^{2};\boldsymbol{\theta}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(88)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">in which <math id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DSM}}(\sigma_{t}^{2};\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">DSM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝛉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DSM}}(\sigma_{t}^{2};\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DSM}}(\sigma_{t}^{2};\boldsymbol{\theta}):=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})-\boldsymbol{s}(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\|^{2}d\sigma^{2}_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DSM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DSM}}(\sigma_{t}^{2};\boldsymbol{\theta}):=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})-\boldsymbol{s}(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\|^{2}d\sigma^{2}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and <math id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}|\mathbf{x}),\mathbf{\pi}(\mathbf{x}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}|\mathbf{x}),\mathbf{\pi}(\mathbf{x}))</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}|\mathbf{x}),\mathbf{\pi}(\mathbf{x}))=D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}|\mathbf{x})\|q(\mathbf{y}_{1}))+\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}|\mathbf{x}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}|\mathbf{x}),\mathbf{\pi}(\mathbf{x}))=D_{\text{KL}}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}|\mathbf{x})\|q(\mathbf{y}_{1}))+\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}|\mathbf{x})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">From Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Thermodynamic Decomposition of Mismatched Entropy). ‣ 3.2 Bounding the Mismatched Entropy with Thermodynamic Diffusion ‣ 3 Variance-Aware Likelihood Estimation of Diffusion models ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{x})}[\log q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{x})}[\log q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{y}_{1})}[\log\pi(\mathbf{x})]+\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})p(\mathbf{x})}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})-\boldsymbol{s}(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\|^{2}d\sigma^{2}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{y}_{1})}[\log\pi(\mathbf{x})]+\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})p(\mathbf{x})}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})-\boldsymbol{s}(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\|^{2}d\sigma^{2}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E89.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})p(\mathbf{x})}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})\|^{2}d\sigma^{2}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})p(\mathbf{x})}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})\|^{2}d\sigma^{2}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(89)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p(\mathbf{y}_{1}|\mathbf{x})p(\mathbf{x})d\mathbf{x}\log\pi(\mathbf{x})d\mathbf{y}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p(\mathbf{y}_{1}|\mathbf{x})p(\mathbf{x})d\mathbf{x}\log\pi(\mathbf{x})d\mathbf{y}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\iint_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}{p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})p(\mathbf{x})}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})\|^{2}d\mathbf{x}d\mathbf{y}_{t}d\sigma^{2}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mo>∬</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\iint_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}{p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})p(\mathbf{x})}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})\|^{2}d\mathbf{x}d\mathbf{y}_{t}d\sigma^{2}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E90.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\iint_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}{p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})p(\mathbf{x})}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})-\boldsymbol{s}(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\|^{2}d\mathbf{x}d\mathbf{y}_{t}d\sigma^{2}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mo>∬</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\iint_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}{p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})p(\mathbf{x})}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})-\boldsymbol{s}(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta})\|^{2}d\mathbf{x}d\mathbf{y}_{t}d\sigma^{2}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(90)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Given a fixed channel <math id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>, we can easily see that <math id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p(\mathbf{x})d\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p(\mathbf{x})d\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> in both sides of (<a href="#A1.E90" title="In Proof. ‣ A.5.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.5 Proof and Remark of Theorems ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">90</span></a>) can be canceled to get</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\log q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\log q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex46.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p(\mathbf{y}_{1}|\mathbf{x})\log\pi(\mathbf{x})d\mathbf{y}_{1}-\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}{p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})\|^{2}d\mathbf{y}_{t}d\sigma^{2}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}p(\mathbf{y}_{1}|\mathbf{x})\log\pi(\mathbf{x})d\mathbf{y}_{1}-\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}{p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})\|^{2}d\mathbf{y}_{t}d\sigma^{2}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E91.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}{p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})-\boldsymbol{s}(\mathbf{y}_{t},\boldsymbol{\theta})\|^{2}d\mathbf{y}_{t}d\sigma^{2}_{t}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}{p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})-\boldsymbol{s}(\mathbf{y}_{t},\boldsymbol{\theta})\|^{2}d\mathbf{y}_{t}d\sigma^{2}_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(91)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">The second term in (<a href="#A1.E91" title="In Proof. ‣ A.5.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ A.5 Proof and Remark of Theorems ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">91</span></a>) corresponds to one-half of the integrated Fisher information of the Gaussian distribution, which is strictly non-negative <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>, we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\log q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\leq\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}|\mathbf{x}),\mathbf{\pi}(\mathbf{x}))+\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}{p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})-\boldsymbol{s}(\mathbf{y}_{t},\boldsymbol{\theta})\|^{2}d\mathbf{y}_{t}d\sigma^{2}_{t}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\log q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\leq\mathcal{H}(p(\mathbf{y}_{1}|\mathbf{x}),\mathbf{\pi}(\mathbf{x}))+\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma^{2}_{1}}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}{p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})}\|\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})-\boldsymbol{s}(\mathbf{y}_{t},\boldsymbol{\theta})\|^{2}d\mathbf{y}_{t}d\sigma^{2}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(92)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">which finishes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.5.4 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (de Bruijn identity with arbitrary noise ( ) ). ‣ 3.5 Training-Free Dequantization with Warm-up Noise ‣ 3 Variance-Aware Likelihood Estimation of Diffusion models ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></h4>

<div id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (de Bruijn identity with arbitrary noise ( ) ). ‣ 3.5 Training-Free Dequantization with Warm-up Noise ‣ 3 Variance-Aware Likelihood Estimation of Diffusion models ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</span>
<span id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathbf{X}}=\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}+\sigma_{t}\boldsymbol{\Psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐗</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚿</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathbf{X}}=\alpha_{t}\mathbf{X}+\sigma_{t}\boldsymbol{\Psi}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X},\boldsymbol{\Psi}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐗</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚿</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X},\boldsymbol{\Psi}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent random vectors, with <math id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\Psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\Psi}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\boldsymbol{\Psi}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝚿</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\boldsymbol{\Psi}]=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cov}(\boldsymbol{\Psi})=\mathbf{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cov}(\boldsymbol{\Psi})=\mathbf{I}</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume the probability density function <math id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{X}</annotation></semantics></math> is twice continuously differentiable and decays sufficiently fast at infinity, and that the Fisher information <math id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}(\mathbf{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}(\mathbf{X})</annotation></semantics></math> exists and is finite. Then,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mathcal{H}\bigl(p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\bigr)\bigg|_{\sigma_{t}^{2}\rightarrow 0^{+}}=\frac{1}{2}\mathcal{J}\big(p(\mathbf{x})\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mathcal{H}\bigl(p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\bigr)\bigg|_{\sigma_{t}^{2}\rightarrow 0^{+}}=\frac{1}{2}\mathcal{J}\big(p(\mathbf{x})\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(93)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the differential Shannon entropy and <math id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Fisher information.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the smoothing properties established in Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ A.4 Lemmas ‣ Appendix A Preliminaries and Reviews ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the distribution <math id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})</annotation></semantics></math> is differentiable with respect to <math id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the integrand in equation (<a href="#S3.E13" title="In Proposition 2 (de Bruijn identity with arbitrary noise ( ) ). ‣ 3.5 Training-Free Dequantization with Warm-up Noise ‣ 3 Variance-Aware Likelihood Estimation of Diffusion models ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>) is both continuous and differentiable in <math id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we may interchange the order of differentiation and integration to obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mathcal{H}\big(p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mathcal{H}\big(p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E94.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\cdot\left(1+\log p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\right)\,d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\frac{d}{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\cdot\left(1+\log p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\right)\,d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(94)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E95.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\left(\Delta_{\tilde{\mathbf{x}}}p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\right)\log p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\,d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{1}{2}\int_{\mathbb{R}^{D}}\left(\Delta_{\tilde{\mathbf{x}}}p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\right)\log p(\tilde{\mathbf{x}})\,d\tilde{\mathbf{x}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(95)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Following the same argument as in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Score Matching as the Small-Noise Limit of KL Divergence). ‣ 3.1 Relationship between Score Matching and KL Divergence ‣ 3 Variance-Aware Likelihood Estimation of Diffusion models ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, this establishes the desired expression, which recovers the special case of isotropic additive noise discussed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">60</a>]</cite>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Improve the Likelihood Estimation Bounds</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our theoretical analysis suggests that different variance functions can lead to varying performance in likelihood estimation. To validate this empirically, we evaluate the effect of different noise schedules, variance functions and datasets on likelihood estimation performance.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">However, in practice, exact numerical evaluation of the integral is generally intractable. A common approach is to use Monte Carlo method to estimate the variance integral in <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DSM}}(\sigma_{t}^{2};\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DSM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DSM}}(\sigma_{t}^{2};\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> during both training and evaluation. Moreover, reducing the variance of the Monte Carlo estimator for the continuous loss objective generally improves the efficiency of optimization. We next summarize our empirical observations on likelihood estimation across different settings.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Variance-Aware Likelihood Bounds</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As mentioned in Section <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Bounding the log-likelihood on Individual Datapoints ‣ 3 Variance-Aware Likelihood Estimation of Diffusion models ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>, denoising score matching <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib79" title="" class="ltx_ref">79</a>]</cite> is typically used as the training objective for diffusion models, serving as a surrogate for approximating the likelihood function <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(\hat{\mathbf{x}};\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, recall that out channel (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2.1 Incremental Gaussian Channel and Maximum Likelihood Estimation ‣ 2 Background ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) is defined as <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})=\mathcal{N}(\alpha_{t}\mathbf{x},\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})=\mathcal{N}(\alpha_{t}\mathbf{x},\sigma_{t}^{2}\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})=-\mathbf{n}/\sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\mathbf{y}_{t}}\log p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})=-\mathbf{n}/\sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the sense that with the score model <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{\boldsymbol{s}}(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta}):=-\hat{\mathbf{n}}(\mathbf{y}_{t},\eta_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})/\sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">:=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\boldsymbol{s}}(\mathbf{y}_{t};\boldsymbol{\theta}):=-\hat{\mathbf{n}}(\mathbf{y}_{t},\eta_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})/\sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the objective takes the following integral form, where the loss is evaluated under varying noise levels:</p>
<table id="A2.E96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DSM}}(\sigma_{t}^{2};\boldsymbol{\theta})=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})}\left[\sigma_{t}^{-2}\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}(\mathbf{y}_{t},\eta_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\|_{2}^{2}\right]\ d\sigma_{t}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DSM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DSM}}(\sigma_{t}^{2};\boldsymbol{\theta})=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})}\left[\sigma_{t}^{-2}\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}(\mathbf{y}_{t},\eta_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\|_{2}^{2}\right]\ d\sigma_{t}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(96)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by approximating the expectation in <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DSM}}(\sigma_{t}^{2};\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DSM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DSM}}(\sigma_{t}^{2};\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> via Monte Carlo estimation. This involves drawing samples <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{t}\sim p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{t}\sim p(\mathbf{y}_{t}|\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> from a tractable Gaussian kernel, which enables efficient estimation of the denoising objective. To estimate the integral over the variance schedule, we apply a second Monte Carlo approximation by uniformly sampling <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> from the interval <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\sigma_{0}^{2},\sigma_{1}^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\sigma_{0}^{2},\sigma_{1}^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>. However, we empirically observe that such an estimator can significantly degrade the optimization process, potentially due to increased variance or poor convergence behaviour. To address this, we reparameterize the objective in terms of a smoother coordinate, namely, the negative log signal-to-noise ratio (log-SNR), which facilitates both numerical stability and analytical tractability.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Even under constrained noise schedules, such as the Variance Preserving (VP) formulation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>, which enforces <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{2}_{t}+\sigma_{t}^{2}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{2}_{t}+\sigma_{t}^{2}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, there remains freedom in how <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> evolve over time <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. To abstract away from specific parameterizations such as VP or VE schedules, we adopt a log-SNR parameterization as the default: <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}:=-\log\text{SNR}(t)=-\log\frac{\alpha_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext>SNR</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}:=-\log\text{SNR}(t)=-\log\frac{\alpha_{t}^{2}}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This reparameterization simplifies the analysis and unifies various diffusion formulations under a single coordinate system. Under this reparameterization, the change of variable from time <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> to negative log-<span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">SNR</span> <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> follows:</p>
<table id="A2.E97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d\eta_{t}}{dt}=\frac{1}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\frac{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}{dt}-\frac{1}{\alpha_{t}^{2}}\frac{d\alpha_{t}^{2}}{dt}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d\eta_{t}}{dt}=\frac{1}{\sigma_{t}^{2}}\frac{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}{dt}-\frac{1}{\alpha_{t}^{2}}\frac{d\alpha_{t}^{2}}{dt}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(97)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">For the VP schedule, this simplifies to:</p>
<table id="A2.E98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d\eta_{t}}{dt}=\frac{1}{\alpha_{t}^{2}\sigma_{t}^{2}}\frac{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}{dt}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d\eta_{t}}{dt}=\frac{1}{\alpha_{t}^{2}\sigma_{t}^{2}}\frac{d\sigma_{t}^{2}}{dt}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(98)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">By setting the noisy process to follow an EDM-like variance-exploding (VE) schedule <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite>, we let <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}^{2}\equiv 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}^{2}\equiv 1</annotation></semantics></math> and parameterize the variance as <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}:=\exp(\eta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}:=\exp(\eta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. This configuration is equivalent to that of NCSNv2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">70</a>]</cite> when <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> follows a geometric sequence interpolating between <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t)=2\log(0.01)+2\log(5000)\,t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.01</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5000</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t)=2\log(0.01)+2\log(5000)\,t</annotation></semantics></math>. Under this specification, the objective in (<a href="#A2.E96" title="In B.1 Variance-Aware Likelihood Bounds ‣ Appendix B Improve the Likelihood Estimation Bounds ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">96</span></a>) reduces to the continuous-time loss proposed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>:</p>
<table id="A2.E99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\infty}(\mathbf{x}):=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}),t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}[\eta^{\prime}(t)\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{y}_{t};t)\|_{2}^{2}]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\infty}(\mathbf{x}):=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}),t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}[\eta^{\prime}(t)\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{y}_{t};t)\|_{2}^{2}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(99)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{\prime}(t)=d\eta_{t}/dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{\prime}(t)=d\eta_{t}/dt</annotation></semantics></math> acts as a natural weighting function. In the above case, this means that <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{\prime}(t)=2\log[5000]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>5000</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{\prime}(t)=2\log[5000]</annotation></semantics></math> and thus that weighted function is a constant. We leave the VE schedule optimization for future works.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly, in the information-theoretic VE formulation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">43</a>]</cite>, i.e., <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{\gamma}=\sqrt{\gamma}\ \mathbf{x}+\mathbf{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>γ</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{\gamma}=\sqrt{\gamma}\ \mathbf{x}+\mathbf{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, our bound recovers the loss integrates over the signal-to-noise ratio <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.E100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}:=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\text{SNR}_{\text{min}}}^{\text{SNR}_{\text{max}}}\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z}_{\gamma},\mathbf{x})}\bigl[\|\mathbf{x}-\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{z}_{\gamma},\gamma)\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]\ d\gamma," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mtext>SNR</mtext><mtext>min</mtext></msub><msub><mtext>SNR</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>γ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}:=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\text{SNR}_{\text{min}}}^{\text{SNR}_{\text{max}}}\mathbb{E}_{p(\mathbf{z}_{\gamma},\mathbf{x})}\bigl[\|\mathbf{x}-\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{z}_{\gamma},\gamma)\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]\ d\gamma,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(100)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where instead of integrating w.r.t. time <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, now integrate w.r.t. the signal-to-noise ratio <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, and where <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\text{SNR}_{\text{max}}}=\gamma(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>SNR</mtext><mtext>max</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\text{SNR}_{\text{max}}}=\gamma(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\text{SNR}_{\text{min}}}=\gamma(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>SNR</mtext><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\text{SNR}_{\text{min}}}=\gamma(0)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">In a more general form, the objective in (<a href="#A2.E96" title="In B.1 Variance-Aware Likelihood Bounds ‣ Appendix B Improve the Likelihood Estimation Bounds ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">96</span></a>) recovers the weighted continuous-time formulation of Eq.(66) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>, where the weighting function is defined as <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(t):=\alpha_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(t):=\alpha_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>; equivalently, this corresponds to scaling the signal coefficient by <math id="A2.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> across time:</p>
<table id="A2.E101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{w}_{\infty}(\mathbf{x}):=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}),t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}[\eta^{\prime}(t)\alpha_{t}^{2}\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{y}_{t};t)\|_{2}^{2}]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>𝜽</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{w}_{\infty}(\mathbf{x}):=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I}),t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}[\eta^{\prime}(t)\alpha_{t}^{2}\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}_{\boldsymbol{\theta}}(\mathbf{y}_{t};t)\|_{2}^{2}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(101)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Moreover, (<a href="#A2.E96" title="In B.1 Variance-Aware Likelihood Bounds ‣ Appendix B Improve the Likelihood Estimation Bounds ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">96</span></a>) can be further unified under the stochastic differential equation (SDE) framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">72</a>]</cite>:</p>
<table id="A2.E102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\mathbf{x}=\boldsymbol{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\,dt+g(t)\,d\mathbf{w}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐰</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\mathbf{x}=\boldsymbol{f}(\mathbf{x},t)\,dt+g(t)\,d\mathbf{w},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(102)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{f}(\mathbf{x},t):\mathbb{R}^{D}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒇</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{f}(\mathbf{x},t):\mathbb{R}^{D}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(t)\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(t)\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> are manually designed noise schedules and <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{w}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{w}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is a standard Wiener process. When the variance function satisfies <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\sigma_{t}^{2}/dt=g^{2}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\sigma_{t}^{2}/dt=g^{2}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, the corresponding loss aligns with the likelihood-weighted score-matching objective <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>]</cite>:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E103"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{SM}}(\boldsymbol{\theta}):=\int_{0}^{T}\frac{g^{2}(t)}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim p(\mathbf{x}),\,\mathbf{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})}\bigl[\|\sigma_{t}\hat{\boldsymbol{s}}(\mathbf{y}_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})+\mathbf{n}\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]\,dt." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>SM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{SM}}(\boldsymbol{\theta}):=\int_{0}^{T}\frac{g^{2}(t)}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim p(\mathbf{x}),\,\mathbf{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})}\bigl[\|\sigma_{t}\hat{\boldsymbol{s}}(\mathbf{y}_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})+\mathbf{n}\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]\,dt.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(103)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.3" class="ltx_p">The same principle extends to deterministic flow-based formulations, including continuous-time ODEs and higher-order probability flows <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>, <a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>, <a href="#bib.bib90" title="" class="ltx_ref">90</a>]</cite> with specific design of the <math id="A2.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{2}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{2}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, the training objective becomes:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E104"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{SM}}^{\eta}(\boldsymbol{\theta}):=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\eta_{0}}^{\eta_{1}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim p(\mathbf{x}),\,\mathbf{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})}\bigl[\|\sigma_{t}\hat{\boldsymbol{s}}(\mathbf{y}_{\eta};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})+\mathbf{n}\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]\,d\eta." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>SM</mtext><mi>η</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{J}_{\text{SM}}^{\eta}(\boldsymbol{\theta}):=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\eta_{0}}^{\eta_{1}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim p(\mathbf{x}),\,\mathbf{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})}\bigl[\|\sigma_{t}\hat{\boldsymbol{s}}(\mathbf{y}_{\eta};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})+\mathbf{n}\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]\,d\eta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(104)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">This reformulation highlights that the loss landscape is intimately linked to the choice of noise schedule, particularly the functional form of <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> as a function of log-SNR <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>. Since both the weighting in the integrand and the resulting likelihood bounds depend explicitly on <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, different scheduling strategies can lead to substantial differences in training dynamics, gradient variance, and overall model performance. In the following, we provide both theoretical and empirical analyses to quantify how the design of <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> influences estimation accuracy, stability, and convergence behaviour.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>The Noise Schedule Matters</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Many practical objectives, including the ones above, are special cases of the likelihood–weighting loss
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>, <a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>, <a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>]</cite>. Let
<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=g(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=g(t)</annotation></semantics></math> be a differentiable, monotone noise parameterization of time
<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> with fixed endpoints <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\min}=g(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\min}=g(0)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\max}=g(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\max}=g(1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a per-example loss, define</p>
<table id="A2.E105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{w}(\mathbf{x}):=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\eta_{\min}}^{\eta_{\max}}w(\eta)\ \mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})}\!\left[\left\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}\bigl(\mathbf{y}_{\eta},\eta;\boldsymbol{\theta}\bigr)\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]\,d\eta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{w}(\mathbf{x}):=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\eta_{\min}}^{\eta_{\max}}w(\eta)\ \mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})}\!\left[\left\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}\bigl(\mathbf{y}_{\eta},\eta;\boldsymbol{\theta}\bigr)\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]\,d\eta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(105)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the noisy input at noise level <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g.,
via a log-SNR parameterization). As shown in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>, the
<em id="A2.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">integral</em> in (<a href="#A2.E105" title="In B.2 The Noise Schedule Matters ‣ Appendix B Improve the Likelihood Estimation Bounds ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">105</span></a>) is invariant to smooth
reparameterizations of <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., to the choice of schedule) so long as the
endpoints <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\min},\eta_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\min},\eta_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> are kept fixed. This invariance extends to
the weighted diffusion loss family <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>]</cite> because the
integrand is measured per unit <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">However, this invariance does <em id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> carry over to the Monte Carlo (MC)
estimator used in evaluation. If we sample <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>, then by change of variables,</p>
<table id="A2.E106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{w}(\mathbf{x})=\frac{1}{2}\ \mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1),\,\mathbf{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})}\!\left[\,w\bigl(\eta(t)\bigr)\ \Bigl|\tfrac{d\eta}{dt}(t)\Bigr|\ \left\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}\!\left(\mathbf{y}_{\eta(t)},\eta(t);\boldsymbol{\theta}\right)\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{w}(\mathbf{x})=\frac{1}{2}\ \mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1),\,\mathbf{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})}\!\left[\,w\bigl(\eta(t)\bigr)\ \Bigl|\tfrac{d\eta}{dt}(t)\Bigr|\ \left\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}\!\left(\mathbf{y}_{\eta(t)},\eta(t);\boldsymbol{\theta}\right)\right\|_{2}^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(106)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">More generally, if we sample directly <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\sim\rho(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\sim\rho(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> over
<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\eta_{\min},\eta_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\eta_{\min},\eta_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math> (with <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> a.e.), then</p>
<table id="A2.E107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{w}(\mathbf{x})=\frac{1}{2}\ \mathbb{E}_{\eta\sim\rho,\ \mathbf{n}}\!\left[\,\frac{w(\eta)}{\rho(\eta)}\ \left\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}\bigl(\mathbf{y}_{\eta},\eta;\boldsymbol{\theta}\bigr)\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{w}(\mathbf{x})=\frac{1}{2}\ \mathbb{E}_{\eta\sim\rho,\ \mathbf{n}}\!\left[\,\frac{w(\eta)}{\rho(\eta)}\ \left\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}\bigl(\mathbf{y}_{\eta},\eta;\boldsymbol{\theta}\bigr)\right\|_{2}^{2}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(107)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">revealing that the <em id="A2.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">noise schedule</em> induces an <em id="A2.SS2.p2.3.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">importance-sampling
distribution</em> <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and a corresponding weighting function <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> related to <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math>, simultaneously. Consequently, while the population loss is invariant
to reparameterization, the <em id="A2.SS2.p2.3.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">variance</em> of the MC estimator (and of its
gradients) depends on <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>. Choosing <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> to better match the integrand can
substantially reduce estimator variance and thus accelerate optimization. In
particular, the variance-minimizing density satisfies the
heuristic proportionality
<math id="A2.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho^{\star}(\eta)\propto\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{X},\mathbf{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})}\!\left[w(\eta)\left\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}(\mathbf{y}_{\eta},\eta;\boldsymbol{\theta})\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]\," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho^{\star}(\eta)\propto\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x}\sim\mathcal{X},\mathbf{n}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})}\!\left[w(\eta)\left\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}(\mathbf{y}_{\eta},\eta;\boldsymbol{\theta})\right\|_{2}^{2}\right]\,</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Variance Reduction with Importance Sampling</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Monte Carlo approximation offers a computationally efficient alternative to exact integration, but typically introduces variance into the training objective. To mitigate this, we adopt both designed and learned importance sampling (IS) strategies, as outlined in Section <a href="#S3.SS4" title="3.4 Variance Reduction with Importance Sampling ‣ 3 Variance-Aware Likelihood Estimation of Diffusion models ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>. As mentioned in Section. <a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2 The Noise Schedule Matters ‣ Appendix B Improve the Likelihood Estimation Bounds ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>, the diffusion model is conducted for all <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\eta_{0},\eta_{1}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\eta_{0},\eta_{1}]</annotation></semantics></math> through an integral. In practice, the evaluation of the integral is time-consuming, and Monte-Carlo methods are used to unbiasedly estimate the objective by uniformly sampling <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, a continuous importance distribution <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> can be proposed for variance reduction. Denote</p>
<table id="A2.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n},\eta;\boldsymbol{\theta}):=\frac{\alpha_{t}^{2}\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}(\mathbf{y}_{\eta},\eta;{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\|_{2}^{2}}{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n},\eta;\boldsymbol{\theta}):=\frac{\alpha_{t}^{2}\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}(\mathbf{y}_{\eta},\eta;{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\|_{2}^{2}}{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">then</p>
<table id="A2.E108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{w}(\mathbf{x};\boldsymbol{\theta})=\mathbb{E}_{\eta\sim\rho(\eta)}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n}}\left[\frac{\mathcal{L}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n},\eta;\boldsymbol{\theta})}{\rho(\eta)}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{w}(\mathbf{x};\boldsymbol{\theta})=\mathbb{E}_{\eta\sim\rho(\eta)}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n}}\left[\frac{\mathcal{L}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n},\eta;\boldsymbol{\theta})}{\rho(\eta)}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(108)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We propose to use two types of importance sampling (IS), and empirically compare them for faster convergence.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.3.1 </span>Designed IS</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In particular, we propose a continuous proposal distributions <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, which is proportional <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\eta}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\eta}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since we have explicit expressions for the density, we utilize inverse transform sampling to design a sampling procedure. Concretely, we take uniform samples of a number <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, and solve the following equation about <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.E109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{Z}\int_{\eta_{0}}^{\eta_{1}}\alpha_{\eta}^{2}\,d\eta=t,\quad Z=\int_{\eta_{0}}^{\eta_{1}}\alpha_{\eta}^{2}\,d\eta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{Z}\int_{\eta_{0}}^{\eta_{1}}\alpha_{\eta}^{2}\,d\eta=t,\quad Z=\int_{\eta_{0}}^{\eta_{1}}\alpha_{\eta}^{2}\,d\eta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(109)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where we have defined maximum time <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> is a normalizing constant.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Uniform Weighting in <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>-Space.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As a canonical example, we consider uniform weighting in the log-SNR domain. In this case, the proposal distribution becomes <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(\eta)\propto\alpha_{\eta}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\eta)\propto\alpha_{\eta}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\quad Z=\int_{\eta_{0}}^{\eta_{1}}\text{sigmoid}(-\eta)\,d\eta=\log\left(\frac{1+e^{-\eta_{0}}}{1+e^{-\eta_{1}}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><mtext>sigmoid</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\quad Z=\int_{\eta_{0}}^{\eta_{1}}\text{sigmoid}(-\eta)\,d\eta=\log\left(\frac{1+e^{-\eta_{0}}}{1+e^{-\eta_{1}}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Also, for squashed hyperbolic tangent, we have:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\quad Z=\int_{\eta_{0}}^{\eta_{1}}\text{sigmoid}(-2\eta)\,d\eta=\frac{1}{2}\log\left(\frac{1+e^{-2\eta_{0}}}{1+e^{-2\eta_{1}}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><mtext>sigmoid</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\quad Z=\int_{\eta_{0}}^{\eta_{1}}\text{sigmoid}(-2\eta)\,d\eta=\frac{1}{2}\log\left(\frac{1+e^{-2\eta_{0}}}{1+e^{-2\eta_{1}}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">To enable inverse transform sampling, we define the antiderivative <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\eta):=\log(1+e^{-\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\eta):=\log(1+e^{-\eta})</annotation></semantics></math>, and set <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{0}=g(\eta_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{0}=g(\eta_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{1}=g(\eta_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{1}=g(\eta_{1})</annotation></semantics></math>. The corresponding cumulative distribution function (CDF) is then:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\eta)=\frac{l_{0}-g(\eta)}{Z},\quad\eta\in[\eta_{0},\eta_{1}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\eta)=\frac{l_{0}-g(\eta)}{Z},\quad\eta\in[\eta_{0},\eta_{1}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Sampling is performed by drawing <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and solving for <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\eta)=u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\eta)=u</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> is smooth and strictly monotonic, this inverse can be computed via root-finding or a precomputed lookup table. The method is similar to the implementation in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>, <a href="#bib.bib90" title="" class="ltx_ref">90</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Uniform weighting in <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-space.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As discussed in Section <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 Variance-Aware Likelihood Bounds ‣ Appendix B Improve the Likelihood Estimation Bounds ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, drawing <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> uniformly from the interval <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> amounts to using the proposal density <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(\eta)=1/\alpha_{\eta(t)}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\eta)=1/\alpha_{\eta(t)}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. With this baseline choice the objective in Eq. (<a href="#A2.E99" title="In B.1 Variance-Aware Likelihood Bounds ‣ Appendix B Improve the Likelihood Estimation Bounds ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">99</span></a>) can be optimized in its native form: each Monte-Carlo sample is simply re-weighted by the factor <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(\eta)=\alpha_{t}^{2}\,\eta^{\prime}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(\eta)=\alpha_{t}^{2}\,\eta^{\prime}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>, which bundles the forward-process weight <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and the Jacobian <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{\prime}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{\prime}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. Although the resulting estimator exhibits higher variance than the importance-sampling schemes introduced earlier, it provides a clear reference point for measuring the effectiveness of less sophisticated designs.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.3.2 </span>Learned IS</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The variance of the Monte-Carlo estimator depends on the learned network <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{n}}(\cdot;\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{n}}(\cdot;\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>. To minimize the variance, we can parameterize the IS with another network and treat the variance as an objective <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>, <a href="#bib.bib90" title="" class="ltx_ref">90</a>]</cite>. Actually, learning <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to learning a monotone mapping. Thus, we can uniformly sample <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, and regard the IS as change-of-variable from <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.E110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{w}(\mathbf{x};\boldsymbol{\psi},\boldsymbol{\theta})=\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n}}\left[\eta^{\prime}(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})\,\mathcal{L}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n},\eta;\boldsymbol{\theta})\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{w}(\mathbf{x};\boldsymbol{\psi},\boldsymbol{\theta})=\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n}}\left[\eta^{\prime}(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})\,\mathcal{L}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n},\eta;\boldsymbol{\theta})\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(110)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{\prime}(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})=d\eta(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})/dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{\prime}(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})=d\eta(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})/dt</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})</annotation></semantics></math> is a monotonic neural network with parameters <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝍</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the variance <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Var}_{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n},t}[\eta^{\prime}(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})\,\mathcal{L}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n},\eta;\boldsymbol{\theta})]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n},t}[\big(\eta^{\prime}(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})\,\mathcal{L}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n},\eta;\boldsymbol{\theta})\big)^{2}]-\big(\mathcal{L}_{w}(\mathbf{x};\boldsymbol{\psi},\boldsymbol{\theta})\big)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>Var</mtext><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Var}_{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n},t}[\eta^{\prime}(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})\,\mathcal{L}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n},\eta;\boldsymbol{\theta})]=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n},t}[\big(\eta^{\prime}(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})\,\mathcal{L}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n},\eta;\boldsymbol{\theta})\big)^{2}]-\big(\mathcal{L}_{w}(\mathbf{x};\boldsymbol{\psi},\boldsymbol{\theta})\big)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{w}(\mathbf{x};\boldsymbol{\psi},\boldsymbol{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{w}(\mathbf{x};\boldsymbol{\psi},\boldsymbol{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> is proved <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite> invariant to <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})</annotation></semantics></math>, we can minimize <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n},t}[\big(\eta^{\prime}(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})\,\mathcal{L}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n},\eta;\boldsymbol{\theta})\big)^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n},t}[\big(\eta^{\prime}(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})\,\mathcal{L}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{n},\eta;\boldsymbol{\theta})\big)^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math> for variance reduction. At this point, we parameterize <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})</annotation></semantics></math> similar to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>. where the network consists of 3 linear layers with weights that are restricted to be positive <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{1},l_{2},l_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{1},l_{2},l_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, which are composed as <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\eta}(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})=l_{1}(t)+l_{3}(\text{sigmoid}(l_{2}(l_{1}(t))))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>sigmoid</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\eta}(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})=l_{1}(t)+l_{3}(\text{sigmoid}(l_{2}(l_{1}(t))))</annotation></semantics></math>. The <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> layer has 1024 outputs, where <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> have a single output.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We therefore postprocess the monotonic neural network as</p>
<table id="A2.E111" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})=\eta_{0}+(\eta_{1}-\eta_{0})\frac{\tilde{\eta}(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})-\tilde{\eta}(0;\boldsymbol{\psi})}{\tilde{\eta}(1;\boldsymbol{\psi})-\tilde{\eta}(0;\boldsymbol{\psi})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})=\eta_{0}+(\eta_{1}-\eta_{0})\frac{\tilde{\eta}(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})-\tilde{\eta}(0;\boldsymbol{\psi})}{\tilde{\eta}(1;\boldsymbol{\psi})-\tilde{\eta}(0;\boldsymbol{\psi})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(111)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where the constants <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{0}=-\log(\text{SNR}_{\text{MAX}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext>SNR</mtext><mtext>MAX</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{0}=-\log(\text{SNR}_{\text{MAX}})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{1}=-\log(\text{SNR}_{\text{MIN}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext>SNR</mtext><mtext>MIN</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{1}=-\log(\text{SNR}_{\text{MIN}})</annotation></semantics></math> define the target SNR range. This construction ensures that <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})</annotation></semantics></math> remains monotonic and bounded. By adjusting the network parameters <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝍</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math> we adapt the time-to-noise mapping <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\mapsto\eta(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\mapsto\eta(t)</annotation></semantics></math> to match regions with higher loss variance, thereby allocating more samples to informative regions of the diffusion trajectory.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS2.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Overhead.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">While this approach seeks the optimal IS, learning <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> adds a lightweight auxiliary network training steps and complex gradient operation through <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝍</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(t;\boldsymbol{\psi})</annotation></semantics></math>, but no extra score-network passes. Hence, we use it mainly to benchmark the optimality of hand-designed IS; more aggressive adaptive schemes following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">39</a>, <a href="#bib.bib90" title="" class="ltx_ref">90</a>]</cite> are compatible.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Log-SNR-Timed Channel with Different Variance Functions</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given the central role of <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> in shaping both the weighting of the loss and the structure of the forward process, it is natural to ask how different functional forms of <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math> affect the overall behaviour of the model. In particular, we investigate how alternative variance functions under the log-SNR parameterization influence the resulting likelihood bound, optimization dynamics, and numerical stability. This section provides both analytical insights and empirical comparisons across several representative schedules. As state in Section <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 Variance-Aware Likelihood Bounds ‣ Appendix B Improve the Likelihood Estimation Bounds ‣ Information Theoretic Learning for Diffusion Models with Warm Start" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, using <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> timing and denoising score matching estimator, the variance weighted objectives are reformulated as:</p>
<table id="A2.E112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DSM}}(\sigma_{t}^{2};\boldsymbol{\theta})=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{n}}\left[\sigma_{t}^{-2}\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}(\mathbf{y}_{t},\eta_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\|_{2}^{2}\right]\ d\sigma_{t}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DSM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DSM}}(\sigma_{t}^{2};\boldsymbol{\theta})=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\sigma_{0}^{2}}^{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{n}}\left[\sigma_{t}^{-2}\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}(\mathbf{y}_{t},\eta_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\|_{2}^{2}\right]\ d\sigma_{t}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(112)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Due to the <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>-timed schedule properties, we replace the time subscript with <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> are deterministic functions of <math id="A2.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> without any hyperparameters.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Logistic Sigmoid.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin with the benchmark variance function <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\eta}^{2}=\mathrm{sigmoid}(\eta):=\frac{1}{1+e^{-\eta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>sigmoid</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\eta}^{2}=\mathrm{sigmoid}(\eta):=\frac{1}{1+e^{-\eta}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is widely adopted in VP-based diffusion models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">40</a>]</cite>. This schedule maps variance smoothly into the unit interval, with most of the variation concentrated around <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\eta}^{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\eta}^{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib90" title="" class="ltx_ref">90</a>]</cite>. Its symmetry and boundedness make it a natural default choice, but also raise questions about its flexibility in capturing tail behaviour and class imbalance. We have the analytic form of the derivative of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\sigma_{\eta}^{2}=(1-\sigma_{\eta}^{2})\sigma_{\eta}^{2}d\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\sigma_{\eta}^{2}=(1-\sigma_{\eta}^{2})\sigma_{\eta}^{2}d\eta</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.E113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DSM}}(\sigma_{t}^{2};\boldsymbol{\theta})=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\eta_{0}}^{\eta_{1}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{n}}\left[(1-\sigma_{\eta}^{2})\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}(\mathbf{y}_{t},\eta_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\|_{2}^{2}\right]\ d\eta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DSM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DSM}}(\sigma_{t}^{2};\boldsymbol{\theta})=\frac{1}{2}\int_{\eta_{0}}^{\eta_{1}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{n}}\left[(1-\sigma_{\eta}^{2})\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}(\mathbf{y}_{t},\eta_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\|_{2}^{2}\right]\ d\eta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(113)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Generalized Logistic Sigmoid.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Then we consider the type I generalized logistic sigmoid function <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite> <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\eta}^{2}=\text{sigmoid}^{a}(\eta)=(\frac{1}{1+e^{-\eta}})^{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mtext>sigmoid</mtext><mi>a</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>a</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\eta}^{2}=\text{sigmoid}^{a}(\eta)=(\frac{1}{1+e^{-\eta}})^{a}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> is strict positive coefficient. We have <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\sigma_{\eta}^{2}=a(1-\text{sigmoid}(\eta))\sigma_{\eta}^{2}d\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>sigmoid</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\sigma_{\eta}^{2}=a(1-\text{sigmoid}(\eta))\sigma_{\eta}^{2}d\eta</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.E114" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DSM}}(\sigma_{t}^{2};\boldsymbol{\theta})=\frac{a}{2}\int_{\eta_{0}}^{\eta_{1}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{n}}\left[\text{sigmoid}(-\eta)\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}(\mathbf{y}_{t},\eta_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\|_{2}^{2}\right]\ d\eta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DSM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mtext>sigmoid</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DSM}}(\sigma_{t}^{2};\boldsymbol{\theta})=\frac{a}{2}\int_{\eta_{0}}^{\eta_{1}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{n}}\left[\text{sigmoid}(-\eta)\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}(\mathbf{y}_{t},\eta_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\|_{2}^{2}\right]\ d\eta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(114)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Squashed Hyperbolic tangent.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Then we consider the Tanh squash function <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\eta}^{2}=\frac{1}{2}(\text{tanh}(\eta)+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>tanh</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\eta}^{2}=\frac{1}{2}(\text{tanh}(\eta)+1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the analytic form of the derivative of <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\sigma_{\eta}^{2}=2(1-\sigma_{\eta}^{2})\sigma_{\eta}^{2}d\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\sigma_{\eta}^{2}=2(1-\sigma_{\eta}^{2})\sigma_{\eta}^{2}d\eta</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.E115" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{DSM}}(\sigma_{t}^{2};\boldsymbol{\theta})=\int_{\eta_{0}}^{\eta_{1}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{n}}\left[(1-\sigma_{\eta}^{2})\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}(\mathbf{y}_{t},\eta_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\|_{2}^{2}\right]\ d\eta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>DSM</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>η</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>𝐧</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐧</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{DSM}}(\sigma_{t}^{2};\boldsymbol{\theta})=\int_{\eta_{0}}^{\eta_{1}}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{n}}\left[(1-\sigma_{\eta}^{2})\|\mathbf{n}-\hat{\mathbf{n}}(\mathbf{y}_{t},\eta_{t};{\boldsymbol{\theta}})\|_{2}^{2}\right]\ d\eta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(115)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>: </span><span id="A2.T5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Specification of related values and objectives under VP schedule. With <math id="A2.T5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(\eta)=\text{sigmoid}(\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>sigmoid</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(\eta)=\text{sigmoid}(\eta)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.T5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{-}=\text{sigmoid}(-\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>sigmoid</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{-}=\text{sigmoid}(-\eta)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.T5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=s^{a/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=s^{a/2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
<div id="A2.T5.5" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:49.8pt;vertical-align:-22.6pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(1.9pt,-0.3pt) scale(1.01134155804584,1.01134155804584) ;">
<table id="A2.T5.5.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A2.T5.5.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T5.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T5.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Formula</span></th>
<th id="A2.T5.5.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T5.5.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Generalized Logistic Sigmoid</span></th>
<th id="A2.T5.5.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.T5.5.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Squashed Hyperbolic tangent</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A2.T5.5.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T5.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding-bottom: 4.0pt;"><math id="A2.T5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
